    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=398&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=rbqj4tr6qcgk8s08ko8088goggssso8": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms at Work We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms at Work [Se nedan för svenska] MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms at Work Position details Recruiting institution: Hanken School of Economics, Department of Management and Organisation Work location: Helsinki, Finland · one position Contract: four-year, full-time doctoral scholarship · 48 months Expected start: 1 February 2027 or by agreement Application deadline: by 11:59 p.m. on 29 October 2026 Doctoral programme: PhD in Management and Organisation Apply: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?o=A_LOJ&list=1&lang=en&rspvt=bx32qk756igw8ww08c0k4sgg0w8w48c Hanken School of Economics, Department of Management and Organisation invites applications for this four-year doctoral scholarship in the EMANAIRE project, PhD project: “AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms at Work”. About EMANAIRE EMANAIRE is a Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Network bringing together 15 doctoral candidates at nine European universities to study how AI is changing work. Its projects examine what happens when generative and agentic AI enters leadership, everyday workflows, team communication, professional learning and career decisions. Across the network, human agency means the practical ability to understand AI-supported decisions, exercise judgement, question outputs and shape how work is organised. Each researcher joins an international cohort, receives supervision across institutions and takes part in three residential schools, methods workshops, monthly research seminars and joint work with organisations beyond academia. Every project includes extensive engagement with industrial partner (e.g. in terms of data collection and development of practice). The doctoral project As AI becomes embedded in everyday work, employees increasingly interact with AI agents, but also encounter AI-mediated contributions from colleagues. Messages may be written, filtered or delivered with AI, while autonomous agents increasingly participate in work processes and collaboration. This doctoral project examines how these developments shape relational aspects of work, (which may include authenticity, trust, social connection, and experiences of loneliness), as people negotiate emerging norms around AI use, disclosure, and appropriate forms of interaction. Through ethnographic research in AI-intensive settings, you will follow relational practices as they evolve over time and identify the mechanisms behind change. The project will develop evidence-based guidance that supports transparency, social connection and responsible AI use in organisational life. Practitioner outputs include AI- aware communication norms, guidance on disclosure and authenticity in AI-assisted exchanges, and leadership practices that protect social connection and prevent relational deterioration. In addition, the doctoral project is expected to advance scientific knowledge in relation to the doctoral topic. Your work Examine how interactions among people, AI agents and AI-mediated communication shape workplace relationships and collaboration. Conduct ethnographic research on how employees make sense of and negotiate AI use in workplace interactions, including norms of disclosure and transparency, and how these processes shape relational aspects of work. Identify the mechanisms through which AI-mediated contributions and autonomous agents reshape relational dynamics, and develop evidence-based guidance for responsible and socially sustainable AI use. Develop AI-aware communication norms and leadership guidance that protect social connection at work. Refine the research questions and design with the supervision team and prepare ethics, data-management and open-science materials. Complete a doctoral thesis and related research outputs under the host doctoral programme and EMANAIRE plan. Take part in local and network-wide training, cohort activities, reviews, dissemination and practitioner engagement. Participate in teaching related activities at the Department of Management and Organisation. Undertake collaboration with the industry partner and a separate academic mobility visit. Contribute to research integrity, equality, responsible AI, open science and FAIR data practices. Supervision, training and mobility Project contact: Emma Nordbäck ( emma.nordback@hanken.fi ). Main supervisor: Associate Professor Emma Nordbäck (Hanken School of Economics). Current DoA plan: The Doctoral researcher is expected to spend a period of time at an industrial partner conducting the ethnographic research and contributing to practice. Academic mobility visit: At least three months at another partner institution of the EMANAIRE network. The researcher will complete at least 60 ECTS of doctoral coursework, including at least 10 ECTS through network-wide provision. EMANAIRE combines local doctoral courses with three residential schools, monthly paper-development seminars, work-package workshops and network reviews. A Personal Career Development Plan will be agreed within the first three months and reviewed every six months. About Hanken School of Economics Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries. It is located in Finland, with campuses in Helsinki and Vaasa. Hanken offers a range of B.Sc., M.Sc., EMBA, PhD, and Executive Development programmes taught mainly in English and Swedish. The School has close ties to the business community and an active alumni network with over 13 800 alumni working in more than 70 countries. The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. The Hanken Masters in Management programme was ranked  #56 by the Financial Times in 2026. Hanken is recognized for its research quality, its international orientation, and its focus on sustainability. Hanken is part of the European ENGAGE.EU European university alliance, that collaborates in the area of doctoral education by creating common practices and offering courses across member universities. The Department of Management and Organisation is recognized for its outstanding research in areas such as organisation studies, human resource management, business ethics and strategic entrepreneurship. The doctoral programme at Hanken is designed as a four-year full-time education, consisting of coursework, thesis work and teaching. Hanken provides comprehensive support throughout the doctoral journey, including supervision, study administration, performance monitoring, and assistance with funding. There is also support for applying for postdoctoral research funding. Who we are looking for Applicants should hold, or be close to completing by the start date, a relevant master's degree or equivalent and demonstrate the potential to undertake independent doctoral research. Research, policy or industry experience relevant to the project is advantageous. In order to be accepted as a Doctoral Researcher at Hanken, applicants must fulfill the formal admission requirements for PhD studies : https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments . A Master’s degree is required. Please ensure that all required attachments are submitted, as they are essential for the academic evaluation of your application. Only applications and attachments sent in through the recruitment system LAURA will be considered. Project-relevant experience and qualifications include: Interest in human side of AI-mediated work, including topics such as communication, collaboration, authenticity, trust, social connection and loneliness. Strong qualitative research skills, including training in ethnography, interviews, observation or longitudinal qualitative research. Ability to study emergent informal norms and relational dynamics in organisational settings, requiring close interaction with participants, strong interpersonal skills, and the capacity to build trust and maintain productive relationships over time. Excellent academic writing and communication skills in English. Employment The scholarship is currently EUR 3755 /month and will be adjusted according to applicable regulations. The salary is based on the university salary system in Finland, which includes free access to employee healthcare as well as pension and holiday bonus. The exact salary level depends on the recruited individual’s qualifications. The salary for the last year differs from the other years and will be according to Hanken’s regular PhD salary. The full-time position has an annual workload of 1,612 hours. During the academic year, we expect you to be present at the department in Helsinki at least three working days per week to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment. Supervision and integration at Hanken The selected candidate will receive close supervision and follow-up from research faculty. The main supervisor is Associate Professor Emma Nordbäck (Hanken School of Economics). In addition, the selected candidate will receive one to two co-supervisors from the EMANAIRE network. The candidate will be integrated into the Department of Management and Organisation and the wider EMANAIRE network. Further information about the doctoral programme and admission requirements is available from Hankens PhD Administration: admissions@hanken.fi How to apply The application should include: Curriculum vitae. Degree certificates and academic transcripts (including diploma supplement if applicable) or evidence that the qualifying degree will be completed before the start date. If your educational certificates are not issued in English submit an official translation to English including copies in the original language. At least two academic or professional references, following the host's stated submission procedure. A 2,000-word research proposal showing independent engagement with this doctoral project and outlining the proposed focus, methods and relevant literature. A declaration covering doctoral status and the MSCA mobility rule. Certificate of language proficiency (see Hanken’s English language requirements at https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/language-requirement/english-language-requirements) Passport copy Academic text (at least 7000 words) Aptitude test or sufficient GPA (see requirements at: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/gpa-or-gmatgre ) Statement of Purpose written on Hankens template, see: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments), Please submit all application materials in English. Submit your application electronically via Hanken’s recruitment database Laura no later than by 11:59 p.m. on October 29th, 2026 (EET) . General instructions for applicants are provided here: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments MSCA eligibility Applicants may be of any nationality. To be eligible for MSCA funding, the selected candidate must, on the first day of MSCA employment: (i) not hold a doctoral degree; candidates who have successfully defended a doctoral thesis but have not yet formally received the degree are not eligible; (ii) comply with the MSCA mobility rule, meaning they must not have resided or carried out their main activity (work, studies, etc.) in Finland for more than 12 months during the 36 months immediately preceding that date, excluding compulsory national service, short stays such as holidays, and time spent in a procedure for obtaining refugee status under the Geneva Convention; and (iii) be enrolled in, or meet the conditions required for timely enrolment in, the doctoral programme leading to the degree specified in this notice. The appointment is conditional on documentary verification of these conditions and fulfilment of the host institution's doctoral admission requirements. More information Questions about the project can be addressed to Emma Nordbäck at emma.nordback@hanken.fi . Questions about the application process can be sent to Hanken’s PhD Administration at admissions@hanken.fi --- På svenska --- MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-medierad kommunikation och samarbetsnormer i arbetslivet Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan, Institutionen för företagsledning och organisation, inbjuder ansökningar till detta fyraåriga doktorandstipendium inom projektet EMANAIRE. Doktorandprojektet har titeln ”AI-medierad kommunikation och samarbetsnormer i arbetslivet” . Om EMANAIRE EMANAIRE är ett Marie Skłodowska-Curie Doctoral Network som samlar 15 doktorander vid nio europeiska universitet för att studera hur AI förändrar arbetslivet. Projektet undersöker vad som händer när generativ och agentisk AI blir en del av ledarskap, dagliga arbetsflöden, teamkommunikation, professionellt lärande och karriärbeslut. Inom nätverket definieras mänsklig handlingsförmåga som den praktiska förmågan att förstå AI-stödda beslut, utöva omdöme, ifrågasätta resultat och påverka hur arbete organiseras. Varje doktorand blir en del av en internationell forskningsmiljö, får handledning över institutionsgränser och deltar i internatskolor, metodworkshoppar, månatliga forskningsseminarier och samarbete med organisationer utanför akademin. Varje projekt inkluderar dessutom aktivit engagemag med industripartner. Doktorandprojektet I takt med att AI blir en integrerad del av det dagliga arbetet interagerar medarbetare allt oftare med AI-agenter och möter AI-medierade bidrag från kollegor. Meddelanden kan skrivas, filtreras eller förmedlas med hjälp av AI, samtidigt som autonoma agenter i allt större utsträckning deltar i arbetsprocesser och samarbete. Projektet undersöker hur dessa utvecklingar påverkar arbetets relationella dimensioner, såsom autenticitet, tillit, social samhörighet eller upplevelser av ensamhet, när människor förhandlar fram nya normer kring AI-användning, transparens och lämpliga interaktionsformer. Genom etnografisk forskning i AI-intensiva miljöer kommer du att följa hur relationella praktiker förändras över tid och identifiera mekanismerna bakom dessa förändringar. Projektet kommer att utveckla evidensbaserade riktlinjer som stödjer transparens, social samhörighet och ansvarsfull AI-användning i organisatoriskt liv. Praktikorienterade resultat inkluderar AI-medvetna kommunikationsnormer, riktlinjer kring transparens och autenticitet i AI-stödda interaktioner samt ledarskapspraktiker som skyddar social samhörighet och motverkar försämrade relationer. Projektet förväntas även bidra med ny vetenskaplig kunskap inom forskningsområdet. Närmare information om arbetsuppgifter, handledning, utbildning och mobilitet samt vem vi söker och anställningsvillkor hittas i den engelska versionen av annonsen. Handledning och integrering vid Hanken Den utvalda kandidaten kommer att få nära handledning och kontinuerlig uppföljning av forskande fakultetsmedlemmar. Huvudhandledare är biträdande professor Emma Nordbäck (Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan). Dessutom kommer den antagna doktoranden att tilldelas en till två bihandledare från EMANAIRE-nätverket . Doktoranden kommer att integreras i Institutionen för ledning och organisation samt i det bredare EMANAIRE-nätverket . Ytterligare information om doktorandprogrammet och antagningskraven finns via Hankens doktorandadministration: admissions@hanken.fi . Ansökan ska innehålla: Curriculum Vitae. Examensbevis och studieutdrag samt vid behov Diploma Supplement. Minst två akademiska eller professionella referenser. En forskningsplan på cirka 2 000 ord. Intyg om uppfyllande av MSCA:s mobilitetsregel. Intyg över engelska språkkunskaper. Kopia av pass. Akademisk text (minst 7 000 ord). Lämplighetstest eller tillräckligt GPA-värde. Statement of Purpose enligt Hankens mall. Samtliga ansökningshandlingar ska lämnas in på engelska. Skicka in din ansökan elektroniskt via Hankens rekryteringsdatabas Laura senast 29 oktober 2026 (EET) . MSCA-behörighet Sökande kan vara av vilken nationalitet som helst. För att vara berättigad till finansiering inom MSCA måste den utvalda kandidaten, på den första dagen av sin MSCA-anställning: Inte inneha en doktorsexamen. Kandidater som framgångsrikt har försvarat sin doktorsavhandling men ännu inte formellt tilldelats doktorsexamen är inte behöriga. Uppfylla MSCA:s mobilitetsregel, vilket innebär att kandidaten inte får ha varit bosatt eller bedrivit sin huvudsakliga verksamhet (arbete, studier etc.) i Finland under mer än 12 månader under de 36 månader som omedelbart föregår anställningens startdatum. Undantag gäller för obligatorisk nationell tjänstgöring, kortare vistelser såsom semester samt tid som tillbringats i en process för att erhålla flyktingstatus enligt Genèvekonventionen. Vara antagen till, eller uppfylla villkoren för att kunna antas inom utsatt tid till, det doktorandprogram som leder till den examen som anges i denna utlysning. Anställningen är villkorad av att dessa krav kan styrkas genom relevant dokumentation samt att värdinstitutionens krav för antagning till forskarutbildningen uppfylls. Application period starts: 2026-09-15 16:19 Application period ends: 2026-10-29 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=398&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=401&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=rbqj4tr6qcgk8s08ko8088goggssso8": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC 06: AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC 06: AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC 06: AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries [Se nedan för svenska] MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC06: AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries Position details Recruiting institution: Hanken School of Economics, Department of Management and Organisation Work location: Helsinki, Finland · one position Contract: four-year, full-time doctoral scholarship · 48 months Expected start: 1 February 2027 or by agreement Application deadline: by 11:59 p.m. on 29 October 2026 Doctoral programme: PhD in Management and Organisation Apply: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?o=A_LOJ&list=1&lang=en&rspvt=bx32qk756igw8ww08c0k4sgg0w8w48c Hanken School of Economics, Department of Management and Organisation invites applications for this four-year doctoral scholarship in the EMANAIRE project, PhD project: “AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries”. About EMANAIRE EMANAIRE is a Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Network bringing together 15 doctoral candidates at nine European universities to study how AI is changing work. Its projects examine what happens when generative and agentic AI enters leadership, everyday workflows, team communication, professional learning and career decisions. Across the network, human agency means the practical ability to understand AI-supported decisions, exercise judgement, question outputs and shape how work is organised. Each researcher joins an international cohort, receives supervision across institutions and takes part in three residential schools, methods workshops, monthly research seminars and joint work with organisations beyond academia. Every project includes extensive engagement with industrial partner (e.g. in terms of data collection and development of practice). The doctoral project What happens to the value and purpose of creative work when people create alongside AI? This project studies how AI agents, AI-mediated processes and platform algorithms reshape co-creation and moral questions in creative industries. It follows employees, freelancers and studios as they negotiate changes to their work and business models. Through ethnographic fieldwork you will research what practitioners value within the activity of making creative work, and how that changes across human, hybrid and automated practices. The project aims to develop a practice-based account of co-creation and offer guidance for organisations and policymakers seeking equitable, responsible and sustainable creative work. Your work Study how AI agents and platform algorithms reshape co-creation, moral questions and business models in creative industries. Conduct ethnographic fieldwork with employees, freelancers and studios. Examine what practitioners value in creative work across human, hybrid and automated practices. Develop a practice-based account and guidance for equitable, responsible and sustainable creative work. Refine the research questions and design with the supervision team and prepare ethics, data-management and open-science materials. Complete a doctoral thesis and related research outputs under the host doctoral programme and EMANAIRE plan. Take part in local and network-wide training, cohort activities, reviews, dissemination and practitioner engagement. Participate in teaching related activities at the Department of Management and Organisation. Undertake collaboration with the industry partner and a separate academic mobility visit. Contribute to research integrity, equality, responsible AI, open science and FAIR data practices. Supervision, training and mobility Project contact: Mikko Vesa ( mikko.vesa@hanken.fi ). Main supervisor: Professor Mikko Vesa (Hanken School of Economics). Current DoA plan: The Doctoral researcher is expected to spend a period of time at an industrial partner conducting the ethnographic research and contributing to practice. Academic mobility visit: At least three months at another partner institution of the EMANAIRE network . The researcher will complete at least 60 ECTS of doctoral coursework, including at least 10 ECTS through network-wide provision. EMANAIRE combines local doctoral courses with three residential schools, monthly paper-development seminars, work-package workshops and network reviews. A Personal Career Development Plan will be agreed within the first three months and reviewed every six months. About Hanken School of Economics Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries. It is located in Finland, with campuses in Helsinki and Vaasa. Hanken offers a range of B.Sc., M.Sc., EMBA, PhD, and Executive Development programmes taught mainly in English and Swedish. The School has close ties to the business community and an active alumni network with over 13 800 alumni working in more than 70 countries. The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. The Hanken Masters in Management programme was ranked  #56 by the Financial Times in 2026. Hanken is recognized for its research quality, its international orientation, and its focus on sustainability. Hanken is part of the European ENGAGE.EU European university alliance, that collaborates in the area of doctoral education by creating common practices and offering courses across member universities. The Department of Management and Organisation is recognized for its outstanding research in areas such as organisation studies, human resource management, business ethics and strategic entrepreneurship. The doctoral programme at Hanken is designed as a four-year full-time education, consisting of coursework, thesis work and teaching. Hanken provides comprehensive support throughout the doctoral journey, including supervision, study administration, performance monitoring, and assistance with funding. There is also support for applying for postdoctoral research funding. Who we are looking for Applicants should hold, or be close to completing by the start date, a relevant master's degree or equivalent and demonstrate the potential to undertake independent doctoral research. Research, policy or industry experience relevant to the project is advantageous. In order to be accepted as a Doctoral Researcher at Hanken, applicants must fulfill the formal admission requirements for PhD studies : https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments . A Master’s degree is required. Please ensure that all required attachments are submitted, as they are essential for the academic evaluation of your application. Only applications and attachments sent in through the recruitment system LAURA will be considered. Project-relevant experience and qualifications include: Interest and knowledge about the creative industries, including tareas such as e.g., media, gaming, music, arts, and design. Strong qualitative research skills, including training in ethnography, interviews, observation or longitudinal qualitative research. Ability to study work practices and ethical dynamics in organisational settings, requiring close interaction with participants, strong interpersonal skills, and the capacity to build trust and maintain productive relationships over time. Excellent academic writing and communication skills in English. Employment The scholarship is currently EUR 3755 /month and will be adjusted according to applicable regulations. The salary is based on the university salary system in Finland, which includes free access to employee healthcare as well as pension and holiday bonus. The exact salary level depends on the recruited individual’s qualifications. The salary for the last year differs from the other years and will be according to Hanken’s regular PhD salary. The full-time position has an annual workload of 1,612 hours. During the academic year, we expect you to be present at the department in Helsinki at least three working days per week to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment. Supervision and integration at Hanken The selected candidate will receive close supervision and follow-up from research faculty. The main supervisor is Professor Mikko Vesa (Hanken School of Economics). In addition, the selected candidate will receive one to two co-supervisors from the EMANAIRE network. The candidate will be integrated into the Department of Management and Organisation and the wider EMANAIRE network. Further information about the doctoral programme and admission requirements is available from Hankens PhD Administration: admissions@hanken.fi . How to apply The application should include: Curriculum vitae. Degree certificates and academic transcripts (including diploma supplement if applicable) or evidence that the qualifying degree will be completed before the start date. If your educational certificates are not issued in English submit an official translation to English including copies in the original language. At least two academic or professional references, following the host's stated submission procedure. A 2,000-word research proposal showing independent engagement with this doctoral project and outlining the proposed focus, methods and relevant literature. A declaration covering doctoral status and the MSCA mobility rule. Certificate of language proficiency (see Hanken’s English language requirements at https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/language-requirement/english-language-requirements) Passport copy Academic text (at least 7000 words) Aptitude test or sufficient GPA (see requirements at: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/gpa-or-gmatgre ) Statement of Purpose written on Hankens template, see: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments), Please submit all application materials in English. Submit your application electronically via Hanken’s recruitment database Laura no later than by 11:59 p.m. on October 29th, 2026 (EET) . General instructions for applicants are provided here: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments MSCA eligibility Applicants may be of any nationality. To be eligible for MSCA funding, the selected candidate must, on the first day of MSCA employment: (i) not hold a doctoral degree; candidates who have successfully defended a doctoral thesis but have not yet formally received the degree are not eligible; (ii) comply with the MSCA mobility rule, meaning they must not have resided or carried out their main activity (work, studies, etc.) in Finland for more than 12 months during the 36 months immediately preceding that date, excluding compulsory national service, short stays such as holidays, and time spent in a procedure for obtaining refugee status under the Geneva Convention; and (iii) be enrolled in, or meet the conditions required for timely enrolment in, the doctoral programme leading to the degree specified in this notice. The appointment is conditional on documentary verification of these conditions and fulfilment of the host institution's doctoral admission requirements. More information Questions about the project can be addressed to Mikko Vesa at mikko.vesa@hanken.fi . Questions about the application process can be sent to Hanken’s PhD Administration at admissions@hanken.fi . --- På svenska --- MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC 06: AI-samskapande, moral och det inre goda i de kreativa näringarna Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan, Institutionen för företagsledning och organisation, inbjuder ansökningar till detta fyraåriga doktorandstipendium inom projektet EMANAIRE. Doktorandprojektet har titeln ” AI-samskapande, moral och det inre goda i de kreativa näringarna ” . Om EMANAIRE EMANAIRE är ett Marie Skłodowska-Curie Doctoral Network som samlar 15 doktorander vid nio europeiska universitet för att studera hur AI förändrar arbetslivet. Projektet undersöker vad som händer när generativ och agentisk AI blir en del av ledarskap, dagliga arbetsflöden, teamkommunikation, professionellt lärande och karriärbeslut. Inom nätverket definieras mänsklig handlingsförmåga som den praktiska förmågan att förstå AI-stödda beslut, utöva omdöme, ifrågasätta resultat och påverka hur arbete organiseras. Varje doktorand blir en del av en internationell forskningsmiljö, får handledning över institutionsgränser och deltar i internatskolor, metodworkshoppar, månatliga forskningsseminarier och samarbete med organisationer utanför akademin. Varje projekt inkluderar dessutom aktivit engagemag med industripartner. Doktorandprojektet Vad händer med värdet och syftet med kreativt arbete när människor skapar tillsammans med AI? Projektet studerar hur AI-agenter, AI-medierade processer och plattformsalgoritmer omformar samskapande, moraliska frågor och affärsmodeller inom de kreativa näringarna. Projektet följer anställda, frilansare och kreativa studior när de hanterar förändringar i sitt arbete och sina affärsmodeller. Genom etnografiskt fältarbete kommer du att undersöka vad yrkesverksamma värdesätter i själva skapandeprocessen och hur detta förändras i mänskliga, hybrida och automatiserade arbetsformer. Projektet syftar till att utveckla en praktikbaserad förståelse av samskapande samt ge vägledning till organisationer och beslutsfattare som vill främja rättvist, ansvarsfullt och hållbart kreativt arbete Närmare information om arbetsuppgifter, handledning, utbildning och mobilitet samt vem vi söker och anställningsvillkor hittas i den engelska versionen av annonsen. Handledning och integrering vid Hanken Den utvalda kandidaten kommer att få nära handledning och kontinuerlig uppföljning av forskande fakultetsmedlemmar. Huvudhandledare är professor Mikko Vesa (Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan). Dessutom kommer den antagna doktoranden att tilldelas en till två bihandledare från EMANAIRE-nätverket . Doktoranden kommer att integreras i Institutionen för ledning och organisation samt i det bredare EMANAIRE-nätverket . Ytterligare information om doktorandprogrammet och antagningskraven finns via Hankens doktorandadministration: admissions@hanken.fi . Ansökan ska innehålla: Curriculum Vitae. Examensbevis och studieutdrag samt vid behov Diploma Supplement. Minst två akademiska eller professionella referenser. En forskningsplan på cirka 2 000 ord. Intyg om uppfyllande av MSCA:s mobilitetsregel. Intyg över engelska språkkunskaper. Kopia av pass. Akademisk text (minst 7 000 ord). Lämplighetstest eller tillräckligt GPA-värde. Statement of Purpose enligt Hankens mall. Samtliga ansökningshandlingar ska lämnas in på engelska. Skicka in din ansökan elektroniskt via Hankens rekryteringsdatabas Laura senast 29 oktober 2026 (EET) . MSCA-behörighet Sökande kan vara av vilken nationalitet som helst. För att vara berättigad till finansiering inom MSCA måste den utvalda kandidaten, på den första dagen av sin MSCA-anställning: Inte inneha en doktorsexamen. Kandidater som framgångsrikt har försvarat sin doktorsavhandling men ännu inte formellt tilldelats doktorsexamen är inte behöriga. Uppfylla MSCA:s mobilitetsregel, vilket innebär att kandidaten inte får ha varit bosatt eller bedrivit sin huvudsakliga verksamhet (arbete, studier etc.) i Finland under mer än 12 månader under de 36 månader som omedelbart föregår anställningens startdatum. Undantag gäller för obligatorisk nationell tjänstgöring, kortare vistelser såsom semester samt tid som tillbringats i en process för att erhålla flyktingstatus enligt Genèvekonventionen. Vara antagen till, eller uppfylla villkoren för att kunna antas inom utsatt tid till, det doktorandprogram som leder till den examen som anges i denna utlysning. Anställningen är villkorad av att dessa krav kan styrkas genom relevant dokumentation samt att värdinstitutionens krav för antagning till forskarutbildningen uppfylls. Kontakt Frågor om projektet: Mikko Vesa mikko.vesa@hanken.fi Frågor om ansökningsprocessen: admissions@hanken.fi Application period starts: 2026-09-16 13:00 Application period ends: 2026-10-29 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=401&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=397&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=rbqj4tr6qcgk8s08ko8088goggssso8": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Management & Organisation / Biträdande professor (tenure track, nivå 1) i företagsledning och organisation",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Management & Organisation / Biträdande professor (tenure track, nivå 1) i företagsledning och organisation We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Management & Organisation / Biträdande professor (tenure track, nivå 1) i företagsledning och organisation The Department of Management and Organization at Hanken School of Economics invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Management & Organization The position is in Helsinki, starting August 1, 2027, or as agreed. Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries, and recognized for its international orientation and outstanding research quality The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. We have close ties to the business community and an active alumni network. Our master's programme is ranked 56 in the Masters in Management 2026 by Financial Times. We are located in Helsinki and Vaasa. Finland is ranked as one of the best-governed countries in the world (Legatum prosperity index, 2023), as well as the happiest country in the world (World Happiness Report 2026). The city of Helsinki ranks as one of the most liveable cities in the world (The Economist 2024). These are thanks to, among others, the high level of equality and safety; free, high-quality education at both primary, secondary, and university levels; affordable healthcare and childcare; and competitiveness and innovativeness of the business sector. The Department of Management & Organization nurtures a strong community of researchers and teachers. We have a strong research climate, reflected in the volume and diversity of research activities, including externally funded projects, publications in highly ranked academic journals, an active community of PhD researchers, and a wide range of societal impact activities. Our goal is to conduct high-quality academic research with corporate and societal relevance. The focus of our research is broad and includes areas such as organizational behaviour, people management/HRM, strategy and strategic management, AI and technology, responsibility and sustainability, and more. Our scholars engage in active collaboration with other universities and business schools around the world. Scholars associated with the subject regularly publish articles in leading international academic journals such as the Journal of Management, Organization Studies, Academy of Management Review, Strategic Management Journal, Journal of International Business Studies, Journal of Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, Human Relations and Journal of Business Ethics . Our diversity is also reflected in our courses and programme at Bachelor, Master and PhD level. The teaching covers issues within organizational behavior, HRM, strategic management, international business, social responsibility and sustainability, and business ethics. At Hanken, our goal is to educate responsible professionals for the global economy and changing society. We embrace Hanken values in teaching and learning, such as openness, equality, and integrity, and promote an innovative learning community that answers to the challenges of the global world, and that efficiently integrates students, faculty, staff, the corporate world, as well as partner organizations and universities. More information about our teaching and research can be found here: https://www.hanken.fi/en/departments-centres/department-management-and-organisation Requirements Applicants must have a doctoral degree (or be very near completion of the doctorate). The degree can be from any relevant discipline provided that the candidate’s research focus is related to the area of management and organization. A focus on organizational behavior or HRM is considered a merit. Candidates will be reviewed based on their research, teaching, institutional service, and societal impact. The main focus will be on the potential to conduct high-quality scientific research, , and the potential to provide high-quality teaching. Research is the most important of the qualification areas followed by teaching, and then, service and societal impact. Applicants for the current position are required to have a fluent command of both English and Swedish. Teaching in Swedish is expected as part of the position's responsibilities. Academic staff at Hanken are expected to carry out and supervise scientific research projects, obtain external funding, provide high-quality academic teaching, closely follow the advances of their field, and participate in service to Hanken, the larger academic community, and society. The full-time position has an annual working time of 1612 hours. During the academic year, it is expected that a minimum average of three days per week is spent at the office in Helsinki to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment, as well as to the collegial community. Hanken offers relocation support for tenure track professors coming outside Finland and expects full-time academic employees to reside and work in Finland. Teaching tasks are allocated based on the curriculum needs of the subject and by considering relevant expertise. Hanken offers multiple pedagogical training opportunities as well as Swedish language training. Salary and other benefits The salary is based on the university salary system in Finland. The exact salary level depends on qualifications and performance. At the assistant professor level, the annual salary range starts from around 60.000 euros (including a holiday bonus). In addition, the employment includes occupational healthcare as well as pension contributions. Hanken will support the appointed person with a research budget and additional rewards for excellence in research and teaching. Research, travel, and teaching development grants can also be applied for. Individuals placed on the Hanken tenure track have the possibility to advance in their career through regular performance assessments, which take into account their merits in all relevant qualification areas of the tenure track system. Interviews Short-listed candidates will be invited to on-site campus visits including an interview and research presentation. Other arrangements are possible for short-listed candidates not based in Europe. For more information For additional information, please contact Professor Mats Ehrnrooth, Head of Department, mats.ehrnrooth@hanken.fi How to apply The application is to be addressed to the Rector and application materials should include: Cover letter CV, including a list of publications (proposed content here ) Personal statement, which includes a description of past research and its scientific quality, academic impact, plans for future research, a description of the candidate’s service to the department and university, and a description of the candidate’s societal impact Copies of no more than five research publications, including a ‘job market’ paper which is an original piece of research by the candidate that constitutes their best research to date Portfolio (e.g., Teaching portfolio template ) Three letters of reference from academic researchers to be submitted directly to Hanken via humanresources@hanken.fi Relevant certificates (degree certificates, language certificates) Please submit all application materials in English. Please note that only applications submitted through the database will be considered. Full applications should be submitted through the link below no later than November 30, 2026 . General instructions for applicants are provided here . Also, read more about Hanken as an employer here . ******** Institutionen för företagsledning och organisation söker en Biträdande professor (tenure track, nivå 1) i företagsledning och organisation Befattningen är placerad i Helsingfors och anställningen börjar 1.8.2027 eller enligt överenskommelse. Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan är en av de ledande handelshögskolorna i Norden, och är erkänd för sin internationella orientering och framstående forskningskvalitet i förhållande till sin storlek. Högskolan är ackrediterad av AACSB, AMBA och EQUIS. Vi har nära band till näringslivet och ett aktivt alumninätverk. Vårt magisterprogram rankas på plats 56 i Financial Times ranking Masters in Management 2026. Vi finns i Helsingfors och Vasa. Finland rankas som ett av de bäst styrda länderna i världen (Legatum Prosperity Index, 2023), samt som världens lyckligaste land (World Happiness Report 2026). Helsingfors rankas som en av världens mest levnadsvänliga städer (The Economist 2024). Detta tack vare bland annat den höga nivån av jämställdhet och trygghet; gratis utbildning av hög kvalitet på både grundskole-, gymnasie- och universitetsnivå; prisvärd hälso- och sjukvård samt barnomsorg; samt näringslivets konkurrenskraft och innovationsförmåga. Institutionen för företagsledning och organisation har en stark gemenskap av forskare och lärare vars forskningsaktiviteter har ett brett fokus som omfattar områden som organisationsbeteende, personalledning/HRM, strategi och strategisk ledning, AI och teknologi, företagsansvar och hållbarhet, med mera. Vi har ett starkt forskningsfokus som återspeglas i en ökande volym och mångfald av forskningsaktiviteter, inklusive externt finansierade projekt, publikationer i högt rankade akademiska tidskrifter, en aktiv gemenskap av doktorander, och olika aktiviteter med social och samhällelig relevans. Våra forskare publicerar regelbundet sin forskning i ledande internationella akademiska tidskrifter som Journal of Management, Organization Studies, Strategic Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Journal of International Business Studies, Journal of Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, Human Relations och Journal of Business Ethics . Vår mångfald återspeglas också i våra kurser och program på kandidat-, magister-, och doktorandnivå. Vår undervisning präglas av variation och täcker frågor inom personaladministration och HRM samt strategi och strategisk ledning, internationellt företagande, ansvar, hållbarhet och företagsetik. Vid Hanken är vårt mål att utbilda ansvarsfulla yrkesutövare för den globala ekonomin och det föränderliga samhället. Vi omfamnar Hanken värderingar i undervisning och lärande, såsom öppenhet, jämlikhet och integritet, och främjar en mångsidig och innovativ lärandegemenskap som svarar på globala utmaningar och som effektivt integrerar studenter, fakultet, personal, näringslivet samt samarbetsorganisationer och universitet. Mer information om forskningen och undervisningen inom ämnet företagsledning finns på: https://www.hanken.fi/sv/institutioner-center/institutionen-foretagsledning-och-organisation Krav Sökande måste ha en doktorsexamen (eller bevisligen vara i slutskedet av sina doktorandstudier). Doktorsexamen kan vara från olika akademiska discipliner förutsatt att kandidatens forskningsfokus är relaterat till området företagsledning och organisation. Ett fokus på organisationsbeteende eller HRM är meriterande. Sökande kommer att granskas baserat på deras forskning, undervisning, institutionstjänstgöring och samhällspåverkan. Huvudfokus ligger på potentialen att bedriva högkvalitativ vetenskaplig forskning och på potentialen att tillhandahålla högkvalitativ undervisning. Forskning är det viktigaste av behörighetsområdena följt av undervisning och sedan gemensamma uppdrag vid universitetet samt samhällelig växelverkan. Sökande förväntas ha flytande kunskaper i både engelska och svenska. Undervisning på svenska förväntas inom ramen för tjänsten. Akademisk personal vid Hanken förväntas bedriva och handleda vetenskaplig forskning, erhålla extern finansiering, tillhandahålla högkvalitativ akademisk undervisning, noggrant följa utvecklingen inom sitt område och bidra till Hanken, den akademiska gemenskapen och samhället. Heltidsbefattningen har en årlig arbetstid på 1612 timmar. Under läsåret förväntar vi oss att du är anträffbar på institutionen i Helsingfors minst tre arbetsdagar i veckan för att aktivt bidra till forsknings- och undervisningsmiljön, samt till arbetsgemenskapen på institutionen. Hanken erbjuder flyttstöd åt forskardoktorer (tenure track) som kommer från länder utanför Finland och förväntar sig att heltidsanställd akademisk personal bor och arbetar i Finland. Undervisningsuppgifter tilldelas utgående från ämnets behov och lärarens expertis. Hanken erbjuder flera pedagogiska utbildningsmöjligheter samt utbildning i svenska språket. Lön och förmåner Lönen baserar sig på lönesystemet för universiteten i Finland. Den exakta lönenivån beror på kvalifikationer och prestationsnivå. På forskardoktornivå är årslönens utgångsnivå cirka 60 000 euro (inklusive semesterpremie). Hanken stöder forskardoktorn med en budget för forskningen. Man kan ansöka om ytterligare forsknings-, rese- och undervisningsutvecklingsanslag. Dessutom ingår företagshälsovård och pensionspremier i anställningen. Hanken belönar excellens inom forskning och undervisning. Personer som anställs på Hankens tenure track har möjlighet att främja sin karriär genom regelbundna prestationsbedömningar som beaktar deras meriter inom alla relevanta kvalifikationsområden i tenure track-systemet Intervjuer Utvalda kandidater kommer att bjudas in till besök på campus som innefattar en intervju och en forskningspresentation. Andra arrangemang kan ordnas för valda kandidater som inte är bosatta i Europa. Tilläggsinformation För ytterligare information, vänligen kontakta professor Mats Ehrnrooth, Prefekt , mats.ehrnrooth@hanken.fi . Hur ansöka Ansökningar riktas till Hankens rektor och ansökningshandlingar ska inkludera följande dokument: Ansökningsbrev CV inklusive en publikationslista (förslag till uppställning här ) Personlig redogörelse som beskriver tidigare forskning och dess vetenskapliga kvalitet, akademiskt inflytande, planer för kommande forskning, en redogörelse över den sökandes aktivitet inom institutionen och den vetenskapliga gemenskapen samt en redogörelse för den sökandes samhälleliga påverkan Max 5 forskningspublikationer, inklusive ett s.k. ’job market paper’ som utgörs av kandidatens mest framstående originalforskning/primärforskning hittills Undervisningsportfölj (t.ex. Teaching portfolio -model ) Tre rekommendationsbrev av akademiska forskare skall skickas in direkt till Hanken via humanresources@hanken.fi Relevanta diplom och intyg (examensintyg, språkintyg) Vänligen lämna in ansökningshandlingarna på engelska. Observera att endast ansökningar inlämnade via rekryteringsdatabasen beaktas. Sista ansökningsdagen är den 30 november 2026. Allmänna instruktioner för sökande finns här . Läs också mer om Hanken som arbetsgivare här . Application period starts: 2026-09-15 16:30 Application period ends: 2026-11-30 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=397&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=398&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=1zgkynaa3tmso0ogsskg84kckswgkok": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms at Work We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms at Work [Se nedan för svenska] MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms at Work Position details Recruiting institution: Hanken School of Economics, Department of Management and Organisation Work location: Helsinki, Finland · one position Contract: four-year, full-time doctoral scholarship · 48 months Expected start: 1 February 2027 or by agreement Application deadline: by 11:59 p.m. on 29 October 2026 Doctoral programme: PhD in Management and Organisation Apply: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?o=A_LOJ&list=1&lang=en&rspvt=bx32qk756igw8ww08c0k4sgg0w8w48c Hanken School of Economics, Department of Management and Organisation invites applications for this four-year doctoral scholarship in the EMANAIRE project, PhD project: “AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms at Work”. About EMANAIRE EMANAIRE is a Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Network bringing together 15 doctoral candidates at nine European universities to study how AI is changing work. Its projects examine what happens when generative and agentic AI enters leadership, everyday workflows, team communication, professional learning and career decisions. Across the network, human agency means the practical ability to understand AI-supported decisions, exercise judgement, question outputs and shape how work is organised. Each researcher joins an international cohort, receives supervision across institutions and takes part in three residential schools, methods workshops, monthly research seminars and joint work with organisations beyond academia. Every project includes extensive engagement with industrial partner (e.g. in terms of data collection and development of practice). The doctoral project As AI becomes embedded in everyday work, employees increasingly interact with AI agents, but also encounter AI-mediated contributions from colleagues. Messages may be written, filtered or delivered with AI, while autonomous agents increasingly participate in work processes and collaboration. This doctoral project examines how these developments shape relational aspects of work, (which may include authenticity, trust, social connection, and experiences of loneliness), as people negotiate emerging norms around AI use, disclosure, and appropriate forms of interaction. Through ethnographic research in AI-intensive settings, you will follow relational practices as they evolve over time and identify the mechanisms behind change. The project will develop evidence-based guidance that supports transparency, social connection and responsible AI use in organisational life. Practitioner outputs include AI- aware communication norms, guidance on disclosure and authenticity in AI-assisted exchanges, and leadership practices that protect social connection and prevent relational deterioration. In addition, the doctoral project is expected to advance scientific knowledge in relation to the doctoral topic. Your work Examine how interactions among people, AI agents and AI-mediated communication shape workplace relationships and collaboration. Conduct ethnographic research on how employees make sense of and negotiate AI use in workplace interactions, including norms of disclosure and transparency, and how these processes shape relational aspects of work. Identify the mechanisms through which AI-mediated contributions and autonomous agents reshape relational dynamics, and develop evidence-based guidance for responsible and socially sustainable AI use. Develop AI-aware communication norms and leadership guidance that protect social connection at work. Refine the research questions and design with the supervision team and prepare ethics, data-management and open-science materials. Complete a doctoral thesis and related research outputs under the host doctoral programme and EMANAIRE plan. Take part in local and network-wide training, cohort activities, reviews, dissemination and practitioner engagement. Participate in teaching related activities at the Department of Management and Organisation. Undertake collaboration with the industry partner and a separate academic mobility visit. Contribute to research integrity, equality, responsible AI, open science and FAIR data practices. Supervision, training and mobility Project contact: Emma Nordbäck ( emma.nordback@hanken.fi ). Main supervisor: Associate Professor Emma Nordbäck (Hanken School of Economics). Current DoA plan: The Doctoral researcher is expected to spend a period of time at an industrial partner conducting the ethnographic research and contributing to practice. Academic mobility visit: At least three months at another partner institution of the EMANAIRE network. The researcher will complete at least 60 ECTS of doctoral coursework, including at least 10 ECTS through network-wide provision. EMANAIRE combines local doctoral courses with three residential schools, monthly paper-development seminars, work-package workshops and network reviews. A Personal Career Development Plan will be agreed within the first three months and reviewed every six months. About Hanken School of Economics Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries. It is located in Finland, with campuses in Helsinki and Vaasa. Hanken offers a range of B.Sc., M.Sc., EMBA, PhD, and Executive Development programmes taught mainly in English and Swedish. The School has close ties to the business community and an active alumni network with over 13 800 alumni working in more than 70 countries. The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. The Hanken Masters in Management programme was ranked  #56 by the Financial Times in 2026. Hanken is recognized for its research quality, its international orientation, and its focus on sustainability. Hanken is part of the European ENGAGE.EU European university alliance, that collaborates in the area of doctoral education by creating common practices and offering courses across member universities. The Department of Management and Organisation is recognized for its outstanding research in areas such as organisation studies, human resource management, business ethics and strategic entrepreneurship. The doctoral programme at Hanken is designed as a four-year full-time education, consisting of coursework, thesis work and teaching. Hanken provides comprehensive support throughout the doctoral journey, including supervision, study administration, performance monitoring, and assistance with funding. There is also support for applying for postdoctoral research funding. Who we are looking for Applicants should hold, or be close to completing by the start date, a relevant master's degree or equivalent and demonstrate the potential to undertake independent doctoral research. Research, policy or industry experience relevant to the project is advantageous. In order to be accepted as a Doctoral Researcher at Hanken, applicants must fulfill the formal admission requirements for PhD studies : https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments . A Master’s degree is required. Please ensure that all required attachments are submitted, as they are essential for the academic evaluation of your application. Only applications and attachments sent in through the recruitment system LAURA will be considered. Project-relevant experience and qualifications include: Interest in human side of AI-mediated work, including topics such as communication, collaboration, authenticity, trust, social connection and loneliness. Strong qualitative research skills, including training in ethnography, interviews, observation or longitudinal qualitative research. Ability to study emergent informal norms and relational dynamics in organisational settings, requiring close interaction with participants, strong interpersonal skills, and the capacity to build trust and maintain productive relationships over time. Excellent academic writing and communication skills in English. Employment The scholarship is currently EUR 3755 /month and will be adjusted according to applicable regulations. The salary is based on the university salary system in Finland, which includes free access to employee healthcare as well as pension and holiday bonus. The exact salary level depends on the recruited individual’s qualifications. The salary for the last year differs from the other years and will be according to Hanken’s regular PhD salary. The full-time position has an annual workload of 1,612 hours. During the academic year, we expect you to be present at the department in Helsinki at least three working days per week to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment. Supervision and integration at Hanken The selected candidate will receive close supervision and follow-up from research faculty. The main supervisor is Associate Professor Emma Nordbäck (Hanken School of Economics). In addition, the selected candidate will receive one to two co-supervisors from the EMANAIRE network. The candidate will be integrated into the Department of Management and Organisation and the wider EMANAIRE network. Further information about the doctoral programme and admission requirements is available from Hankens PhD Administration: admissions@hanken.fi How to apply The application should include: Curriculum vitae. Degree certificates and academic transcripts (including diploma supplement if applicable) or evidence that the qualifying degree will be completed before the start date. If your educational certificates are not issued in English submit an official translation to English including copies in the original language. At least two academic or professional references, following the host's stated submission procedure. A 2,000-word research proposal showing independent engagement with this doctoral project and outlining the proposed focus, methods and relevant literature. A declaration covering doctoral status and the MSCA mobility rule. Certificate of language proficiency (see Hanken’s English language requirements at https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/language-requirement/english-language-requirements) Passport copy Academic text (at least 7000 words) Aptitude test or sufficient GPA (see requirements at: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/gpa-or-gmatgre ) Statement of Purpose written on Hankens template, see: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments), Please submit all application materials in English. Submit your application electronically via Hanken’s recruitment database Laura no later than by 11:59 p.m. on October 29th, 2026 (EET) . General instructions for applicants are provided here: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments MSCA eligibility Applicants may be of any nationality. To be eligible for MSCA funding, the selected candidate must, on the first day of MSCA employment: (i) not hold a doctoral degree; candidates who have successfully defended a doctoral thesis but have not yet formally received the degree are not eligible; (ii) comply with the MSCA mobility rule, meaning they must not have resided or carried out their main activity (work, studies, etc.) in Finland for more than 12 months during the 36 months immediately preceding that date, excluding compulsory national service, short stays such as holidays, and time spent in a procedure for obtaining refugee status under the Geneva Convention; and (iii) be enrolled in, or meet the conditions required for timely enrolment in, the doctoral programme leading to the degree specified in this notice. The appointment is conditional on documentary verification of these conditions and fulfilment of the host institution's doctoral admission requirements. More information Questions about the project can be addressed to Emma Nordbäck at emma.nordback@hanken.fi . Questions about the application process can be sent to Hanken’s PhD Administration at admissions@hanken.fi --- På svenska --- MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-medierad kommunikation och samarbetsnormer i arbetslivet Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan, Institutionen för företagsledning och organisation, inbjuder ansökningar till detta fyraåriga doktorandstipendium inom projektet EMANAIRE. Doktorandprojektet har titeln ”AI-medierad kommunikation och samarbetsnormer i arbetslivet” . Om EMANAIRE EMANAIRE är ett Marie Skłodowska-Curie Doctoral Network som samlar 15 doktorander vid nio europeiska universitet för att studera hur AI förändrar arbetslivet. Projektet undersöker vad som händer när generativ och agentisk AI blir en del av ledarskap, dagliga arbetsflöden, teamkommunikation, professionellt lärande och karriärbeslut. Inom nätverket definieras mänsklig handlingsförmåga som den praktiska förmågan att förstå AI-stödda beslut, utöva omdöme, ifrågasätta resultat och påverka hur arbete organiseras. Varje doktorand blir en del av en internationell forskningsmiljö, får handledning över institutionsgränser och deltar i internatskolor, metodworkshoppar, månatliga forskningsseminarier och samarbete med organisationer utanför akademin. Varje projekt inkluderar dessutom aktivit engagemag med industripartner. Doktorandprojektet I takt med att AI blir en integrerad del av det dagliga arbetet interagerar medarbetare allt oftare med AI-agenter och möter AI-medierade bidrag från kollegor. Meddelanden kan skrivas, filtreras eller förmedlas med hjälp av AI, samtidigt som autonoma agenter i allt större utsträckning deltar i arbetsprocesser och samarbete. Projektet undersöker hur dessa utvecklingar påverkar arbetets relationella dimensioner, såsom autenticitet, tillit, social samhörighet eller upplevelser av ensamhet, när människor förhandlar fram nya normer kring AI-användning, transparens och lämpliga interaktionsformer. Genom etnografisk forskning i AI-intensiva miljöer kommer du att följa hur relationella praktiker förändras över tid och identifiera mekanismerna bakom dessa förändringar. Projektet kommer att utveckla evidensbaserade riktlinjer som stödjer transparens, social samhörighet och ansvarsfull AI-användning i organisatoriskt liv. Praktikorienterade resultat inkluderar AI-medvetna kommunikationsnormer, riktlinjer kring transparens och autenticitet i AI-stödda interaktioner samt ledarskapspraktiker som skyddar social samhörighet och motverkar försämrade relationer. Projektet förväntas även bidra med ny vetenskaplig kunskap inom forskningsområdet. Närmare information om arbetsuppgifter, handledning, utbildning och mobilitet samt vem vi söker och anställningsvillkor hittas i den engelska versionen av annonsen. Handledning och integrering vid Hanken Den utvalda kandidaten kommer att få nära handledning och kontinuerlig uppföljning av forskande fakultetsmedlemmar. Huvudhandledare är biträdande professor Emma Nordbäck (Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan). Dessutom kommer den antagna doktoranden att tilldelas en till två bihandledare från EMANAIRE-nätverket . Doktoranden kommer att integreras i Institutionen för ledning och organisation samt i det bredare EMANAIRE-nätverket . Ytterligare information om doktorandprogrammet och antagningskraven finns via Hankens doktorandadministration: admissions@hanken.fi . Ansökan ska innehålla: Curriculum Vitae. Examensbevis och studieutdrag samt vid behov Diploma Supplement. Minst två akademiska eller professionella referenser. En forskningsplan på cirka 2 000 ord. Intyg om uppfyllande av MSCA:s mobilitetsregel. Intyg över engelska språkkunskaper. Kopia av pass. Akademisk text (minst 7 000 ord). Lämplighetstest eller tillräckligt GPA-värde. Statement of Purpose enligt Hankens mall. Samtliga ansökningshandlingar ska lämnas in på engelska. Skicka in din ansökan elektroniskt via Hankens rekryteringsdatabas Laura senast 29 oktober 2026 (EET) . MSCA-behörighet Sökande kan vara av vilken nationalitet som helst. För att vara berättigad till finansiering inom MSCA måste den utvalda kandidaten, på den första dagen av sin MSCA-anställning: Inte inneha en doktorsexamen. Kandidater som framgångsrikt har försvarat sin doktorsavhandling men ännu inte formellt tilldelats doktorsexamen är inte behöriga. Uppfylla MSCA:s mobilitetsregel, vilket innebär att kandidaten inte får ha varit bosatt eller bedrivit sin huvudsakliga verksamhet (arbete, studier etc.) i Finland under mer än 12 månader under de 36 månader som omedelbart föregår anställningens startdatum. Undantag gäller för obligatorisk nationell tjänstgöring, kortare vistelser såsom semester samt tid som tillbringats i en process för att erhålla flyktingstatus enligt Genèvekonventionen. Vara antagen till, eller uppfylla villkoren för att kunna antas inom utsatt tid till, det doktorandprogram som leder till den examen som anges i denna utlysning. Anställningen är villkorad av att dessa krav kan styrkas genom relevant dokumentation samt att värdinstitutionens krav för antagning till forskarutbildningen uppfylls. Application period starts: 2026-09-15 16:19 Application period ends: 2026-10-29 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=398&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=401&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=1zgkynaa3tmso0ogsskg84kckswgkok": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC 06: AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC 06: AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC 06: AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries [Se nedan för svenska] MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC06: AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries Position details Recruiting institution: Hanken School of Economics, Department of Management and Organisation Work location: Helsinki, Finland · one position Contract: four-year, full-time doctoral scholarship · 48 months Expected start: 1 February 2027 or by agreement Application deadline: by 11:59 p.m. on 29 October 2026 Doctoral programme: PhD in Management and Organisation Apply: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?o=A_LOJ&list=1&lang=en&rspvt=bx32qk756igw8ww08c0k4sgg0w8w48c Hanken School of Economics, Department of Management and Organisation invites applications for this four-year doctoral scholarship in the EMANAIRE project, PhD project: “AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries”. About EMANAIRE EMANAIRE is a Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Network bringing together 15 doctoral candidates at nine European universities to study how AI is changing work. Its projects examine what happens when generative and agentic AI enters leadership, everyday workflows, team communication, professional learning and career decisions. Across the network, human agency means the practical ability to understand AI-supported decisions, exercise judgement, question outputs and shape how work is organised. Each researcher joins an international cohort, receives supervision across institutions and takes part in three residential schools, methods workshops, monthly research seminars and joint work with organisations beyond academia. Every project includes extensive engagement with industrial partner (e.g. in terms of data collection and development of practice). The doctoral project What happens to the value and purpose of creative work when people create alongside AI? This project studies how AI agents, AI-mediated processes and platform algorithms reshape co-creation and moral questions in creative industries. It follows employees, freelancers and studios as they negotiate changes to their work and business models. Through ethnographic fieldwork you will research what practitioners value within the activity of making creative work, and how that changes across human, hybrid and automated practices. The project aims to develop a practice-based account of co-creation and offer guidance for organisations and policymakers seeking equitable, responsible and sustainable creative work. Your work Study how AI agents and platform algorithms reshape co-creation, moral questions and business models in creative industries. Conduct ethnographic fieldwork with employees, freelancers and studios. Examine what practitioners value in creative work across human, hybrid and automated practices. Develop a practice-based account and guidance for equitable, responsible and sustainable creative work. Refine the research questions and design with the supervision team and prepare ethics, data-management and open-science materials. Complete a doctoral thesis and related research outputs under the host doctoral programme and EMANAIRE plan. Take part in local and network-wide training, cohort activities, reviews, dissemination and practitioner engagement. Participate in teaching related activities at the Department of Management and Organisation. Undertake collaboration with the industry partner and a separate academic mobility visit. Contribute to research integrity, equality, responsible AI, open science and FAIR data practices. Supervision, training and mobility Project contact: Mikko Vesa ( mikko.vesa@hanken.fi ). Main supervisor: Professor Mikko Vesa (Hanken School of Economics). Current DoA plan: The Doctoral researcher is expected to spend a period of time at an industrial partner conducting the ethnographic research and contributing to practice. Academic mobility visit: At least three months at another partner institution of the EMANAIRE network . The researcher will complete at least 60 ECTS of doctoral coursework, including at least 10 ECTS through network-wide provision. EMANAIRE combines local doctoral courses with three residential schools, monthly paper-development seminars, work-package workshops and network reviews. A Personal Career Development Plan will be agreed within the first three months and reviewed every six months. About Hanken School of Economics Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries. It is located in Finland, with campuses in Helsinki and Vaasa. Hanken offers a range of B.Sc., M.Sc., EMBA, PhD, and Executive Development programmes taught mainly in English and Swedish. The School has close ties to the business community and an active alumni network with over 13 800 alumni working in more than 70 countries. The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. The Hanken Masters in Management programme was ranked  #56 by the Financial Times in 2026. Hanken is recognized for its research quality, its international orientation, and its focus on sustainability. Hanken is part of the European ENGAGE.EU European university alliance, that collaborates in the area of doctoral education by creating common practices and offering courses across member universities. The Department of Management and Organisation is recognized for its outstanding research in areas such as organisation studies, human resource management, business ethics and strategic entrepreneurship. The doctoral programme at Hanken is designed as a four-year full-time education, consisting of coursework, thesis work and teaching. Hanken provides comprehensive support throughout the doctoral journey, including supervision, study administration, performance monitoring, and assistance with funding. There is also support for applying for postdoctoral research funding. Who we are looking for Applicants should hold, or be close to completing by the start date, a relevant master's degree or equivalent and demonstrate the potential to undertake independent doctoral research. Research, policy or industry experience relevant to the project is advantageous. In order to be accepted as a Doctoral Researcher at Hanken, applicants must fulfill the formal admission requirements for PhD studies : https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments . A Master’s degree is required. Please ensure that all required attachments are submitted, as they are essential for the academic evaluation of your application. Only applications and attachments sent in through the recruitment system LAURA will be considered. Project-relevant experience and qualifications include: Interest and knowledge about the creative industries, including tareas such as e.g., media, gaming, music, arts, and design. Strong qualitative research skills, including training in ethnography, interviews, observation or longitudinal qualitative research. Ability to study work practices and ethical dynamics in organisational settings, requiring close interaction with participants, strong interpersonal skills, and the capacity to build trust and maintain productive relationships over time. Excellent academic writing and communication skills in English. Employment The scholarship is currently EUR 3755 /month and will be adjusted according to applicable regulations. The salary is based on the university salary system in Finland, which includes free access to employee healthcare as well as pension and holiday bonus. The exact salary level depends on the recruited individual’s qualifications. The salary for the last year differs from the other years and will be according to Hanken’s regular PhD salary. The full-time position has an annual workload of 1,612 hours. During the academic year, we expect you to be present at the department in Helsinki at least three working days per week to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment. Supervision and integration at Hanken The selected candidate will receive close supervision and follow-up from research faculty. The main supervisor is Professor Mikko Vesa (Hanken School of Economics). In addition, the selected candidate will receive one to two co-supervisors from the EMANAIRE network. The candidate will be integrated into the Department of Management and Organisation and the wider EMANAIRE network. Further information about the doctoral programme and admission requirements is available from Hankens PhD Administration: admissions@hanken.fi . How to apply The application should include: Curriculum vitae. Degree certificates and academic transcripts (including diploma supplement if applicable) or evidence that the qualifying degree will be completed before the start date. If your educational certificates are not issued in English submit an official translation to English including copies in the original language. At least two academic or professional references, following the host's stated submission procedure. A 2,000-word research proposal showing independent engagement with this doctoral project and outlining the proposed focus, methods and relevant literature. A declaration covering doctoral status and the MSCA mobility rule. Certificate of language proficiency (see Hanken’s English language requirements at https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/language-requirement/english-language-requirements) Passport copy Academic text (at least 7000 words) Aptitude test or sufficient GPA (see requirements at: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/gpa-or-gmatgre ) Statement of Purpose written on Hankens template, see: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments), Please submit all application materials in English. Submit your application electronically via Hanken’s recruitment database Laura no later than by 11:59 p.m. on October 29th, 2026 (EET) . General instructions for applicants are provided here: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments MSCA eligibility Applicants may be of any nationality. To be eligible for MSCA funding, the selected candidate must, on the first day of MSCA employment: (i) not hold a doctoral degree; candidates who have successfully defended a doctoral thesis but have not yet formally received the degree are not eligible; (ii) comply with the MSCA mobility rule, meaning they must not have resided or carried out their main activity (work, studies, etc.) in Finland for more than 12 months during the 36 months immediately preceding that date, excluding compulsory national service, short stays such as holidays, and time spent in a procedure for obtaining refugee status under the Geneva Convention; and (iii) be enrolled in, or meet the conditions required for timely enrolment in, the doctoral programme leading to the degree specified in this notice. The appointment is conditional on documentary verification of these conditions and fulfilment of the host institution's doctoral admission requirements. More information Questions about the project can be addressed to Mikko Vesa at mikko.vesa@hanken.fi . Questions about the application process can be sent to Hanken’s PhD Administration at admissions@hanken.fi . --- På svenska --- MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC 06: AI-samskapande, moral och det inre goda i de kreativa näringarna Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan, Institutionen för företagsledning och organisation, inbjuder ansökningar till detta fyraåriga doktorandstipendium inom projektet EMANAIRE. Doktorandprojektet har titeln ” AI-samskapande, moral och det inre goda i de kreativa näringarna ” . Om EMANAIRE EMANAIRE är ett Marie Skłodowska-Curie Doctoral Network som samlar 15 doktorander vid nio europeiska universitet för att studera hur AI förändrar arbetslivet. Projektet undersöker vad som händer när generativ och agentisk AI blir en del av ledarskap, dagliga arbetsflöden, teamkommunikation, professionellt lärande och karriärbeslut. Inom nätverket definieras mänsklig handlingsförmåga som den praktiska förmågan att förstå AI-stödda beslut, utöva omdöme, ifrågasätta resultat och påverka hur arbete organiseras. Varje doktorand blir en del av en internationell forskningsmiljö, får handledning över institutionsgränser och deltar i internatskolor, metodworkshoppar, månatliga forskningsseminarier och samarbete med organisationer utanför akademin. Varje projekt inkluderar dessutom aktivit engagemag med industripartner. Doktorandprojektet Vad händer med värdet och syftet med kreativt arbete när människor skapar tillsammans med AI? Projektet studerar hur AI-agenter, AI-medierade processer och plattformsalgoritmer omformar samskapande, moraliska frågor och affärsmodeller inom de kreativa näringarna. Projektet följer anställda, frilansare och kreativa studior när de hanterar förändringar i sitt arbete och sina affärsmodeller. Genom etnografiskt fältarbete kommer du att undersöka vad yrkesverksamma värdesätter i själva skapandeprocessen och hur detta förändras i mänskliga, hybrida och automatiserade arbetsformer. Projektet syftar till att utveckla en praktikbaserad förståelse av samskapande samt ge vägledning till organisationer och beslutsfattare som vill främja rättvist, ansvarsfullt och hållbart kreativt arbete Närmare information om arbetsuppgifter, handledning, utbildning och mobilitet samt vem vi söker och anställningsvillkor hittas i den engelska versionen av annonsen. Handledning och integrering vid Hanken Den utvalda kandidaten kommer att få nära handledning och kontinuerlig uppföljning av forskande fakultetsmedlemmar. Huvudhandledare är professor Mikko Vesa (Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan). Dessutom kommer den antagna doktoranden att tilldelas en till två bihandledare från EMANAIRE-nätverket . Doktoranden kommer att integreras i Institutionen för ledning och organisation samt i det bredare EMANAIRE-nätverket . Ytterligare information om doktorandprogrammet och antagningskraven finns via Hankens doktorandadministration: admissions@hanken.fi . Ansökan ska innehålla: Curriculum Vitae. Examensbevis och studieutdrag samt vid behov Diploma Supplement. Minst två akademiska eller professionella referenser. En forskningsplan på cirka 2 000 ord. Intyg om uppfyllande av MSCA:s mobilitetsregel. Intyg över engelska språkkunskaper. Kopia av pass. Akademisk text (minst 7 000 ord). Lämplighetstest eller tillräckligt GPA-värde. Statement of Purpose enligt Hankens mall. Samtliga ansökningshandlingar ska lämnas in på engelska. Skicka in din ansökan elektroniskt via Hankens rekryteringsdatabas Laura senast 29 oktober 2026 (EET) . MSCA-behörighet Sökande kan vara av vilken nationalitet som helst. För att vara berättigad till finansiering inom MSCA måste den utvalda kandidaten, på den första dagen av sin MSCA-anställning: Inte inneha en doktorsexamen. Kandidater som framgångsrikt har försvarat sin doktorsavhandling men ännu inte formellt tilldelats doktorsexamen är inte behöriga. Uppfylla MSCA:s mobilitetsregel, vilket innebär att kandidaten inte får ha varit bosatt eller bedrivit sin huvudsakliga verksamhet (arbete, studier etc.) i Finland under mer än 12 månader under de 36 månader som omedelbart föregår anställningens startdatum. Undantag gäller för obligatorisk nationell tjänstgöring, kortare vistelser såsom semester samt tid som tillbringats i en process för att erhålla flyktingstatus enligt Genèvekonventionen. Vara antagen till, eller uppfylla villkoren för att kunna antas inom utsatt tid till, det doktorandprogram som leder till den examen som anges i denna utlysning. Anställningen är villkorad av att dessa krav kan styrkas genom relevant dokumentation samt att värdinstitutionens krav för antagning till forskarutbildningen uppfylls. Kontakt Frågor om projektet: Mikko Vesa mikko.vesa@hanken.fi Frågor om ansökningsprocessen: admissions@hanken.fi Application period starts: 2026-09-16 13:00 Application period ends: 2026-10-29 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=401&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=406&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=1zgkynaa3tmso0ogsskg84kckswgkok": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Sustainable and Resilient Freight Transport Systems",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Sustainable and Resilient Freight Transport Systems We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Postdoctoral Researcher in Sustainable and Resilient Freight Transport Systems [Se nedan för svenska] The Hanken School of Economics is looking for a postdoctoral researcher as a project researcher for 8 months to conduct research in the project S ociety Quest for a Resilient and Sustainable Nordic Freight Transport System Funded by the Peter Wallenberg Foundation, the project explores how to strengthen the resilience and environmental sustainability of Nordic freight transport and supply chains. Through parallel Society Quest processes in Finland and Sweden, researchers and societal stakeholders will jointly identify key challenges and develop priorities for future research, development, and Nordic collaboration. Society Quest is a structured co-creation method in which researchers, industry and public-sector actors move step by step from articulating a shared societal challenge to concrete directions for joint action. The position offers a unique opportunity to develop both your academic profile and your experience of working at the interface between research and practice. Postdoc responsibilities: Plan and carry out the Finnish Society Quest, in close collaboration with the Hanken and Linköping University research teams and supporting the Swedish implementation of the Society Quest. Map and engage relevant stakeholders across industry, public authorities, transport infrastructure actors, and the research community. Recruit Society Quest participants and coordinate stakeholder engagement Contribute to the design and facilitation of Society Quest co-creation workshops addressing resilient and environmentally sustainable freight transport. Systematically document and analyze findings in cooperation with the project researchers. Contribute to project dissemination. Preparation of journal manuscript(s) based on project results. The position includes some teaching responsibilities, up to 15 % of work time The successful candidate is expected to have: A doctoral degree in supply chain management, logistics, transportation, sustainability, or another relevant field. Knowledge of, or a strong research interest in, supply chain resilience, sustainable transport, freight transport, or closely related topics. Experience with qualitative and/or participatory research methods, for example, interviews, workshops, focus groups, co-creation, or stakeholder-engaged research. The ability to independently organize and carry out empirical research, including stakeholder identification, recruitment, data collection, documentation, and analysis. Strong stakeholder engagement and communication skills, with the ability to work with both academic and non-academic actors. Excellent written and oral English-language skills. Considered an advantage: Existing experience interacting with companies, public authorities, infrastructure actors, or other societal stakeholders. Experience with workshop facilitation or co-creation methodologies. Knowledge of resilience and sustainability research and their intersection. Finnish and/or Swedish language skills. Existing high-quality academic publications Teaching experience Industry experience Through the position, you will have the opportunity to: Contribute to a Nordic research project and shape its implementation. Develop expertise in resilient and sustainable freight transport. Build networks with academic, industry, and public-sector actors in Finland and Sweden. Gain experience in co-creation, stakeholder engagement, and cross-national research. Contribute to academic publications, societal impact, and the development of future research. Gain academic teaching experience. Eligibility criteria: Eligibility requirements: Applicants for this position are required to have (a) a PhD degree in a relevant subject and (b) a fluent command of English. Applicants close to their PhD defense can be considered if the defense date is decided. Possibility to start latest by February 2027. The position is for 8 months, depending on when you can start (earliest start: January 2027). By joining the Supply Chain Management & Social Responsibility subject at Hanken, you will benefit from and contribute to a thriving scientific environment at a triple crown-accredited university business school (AACSB, EQUIS, AMBA accreditations), becoming part of a group of highly active researchers with high productivity in publishing, numerous global projects, and a strong international profile. The annual working time in this position is 1612 hours. The location of the positions is in Helsinki ( https://www.hel.fi/en ), and we expect you to move to Finland. The salary for the project researcher is based on the university salary system in Finland (including employee healthcare as well as pension and holiday contributions); the exact salary level depends upon the recruited individual’s qualifications and performance. The entry-level salary is in the range of 46.800 - 52.500 euro/year. Benefits include occupational health care. The application should include the following attachments: Motivation letter stating how you’d contribute to the project CV incl. min. 2 references who can be contacted for recommendations PhD degree certificate Publication list incl. working doi links to selected, max 5 recent publications (or if links don’t work, separately submitted publications in pdf form) The application shall be submitted electronically to Hanken’s recruitment database Laura no later than November 16 th 2026 . In addition, other relevant documents (e.g. certificates, recommendations) may be submitted with the application. Please indicate when you would be able to start in the position if you should be selected. Enquiries may be directed to the project team: Associate Professor Anna Aminoff, anna.aminoff@hanken.fi Assistant Professor Helleke Heikkinen, helleke.heikkinen@hanken.fi The Hanken School of Economics reserves the right, for justified reasons, to leave the position open, to extend the application period, and to consider candidates who have not submitted applications during the application period. Hanken School of Economics reserves the right to close the application period early if a suitable candidate is identified and appointed. Further information: Project profiles under the ongoing projects of the HUMLOG Institute at http://www.hanken.fi/humloginstitute Hanken School of Economics: https://www.hanken.fi -- På svenska-- Postdoktoral forskare i hållbara och resilienta godstransportsystem Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan söker en postdoktoral forskare som projektforskare för 8 månader för att bedriva forskning inom projektet Samhällets strävan efter ett resilient och hållbart nordiskt godstransportsystem (Society Quest for a Resilient and Sustainable Nordic Freight Transport System). Projektet finansieras av Peter Wallenbergstiftelsen och undersöker hur resiliensen och den miljömässiga hållbarheten i nordiska godstransporter och försörjningskedjor kan stärkas. Genom parallella Society Quest-processer i Finland och Sverige kommer forskare och samhällsaktörer gemensamt att identifiera centrala utmaningar och utveckla prioriteringar för framtida forskning, utveckling och nordiskt samarbete. Society Quest är en strukturerad metod för samskapande där forskare, näringsliv och offentliga aktörer stegvis går från att formulera en gemensam samhällsutmaning till konkreta riktlinjer för gemensamma åtgärder. Tjänsten erbjuder en unik möjlighet att utveckla både din akademiska profil och din erfarenhet av att arbeta i gränslandet mellan forskning och praktik. Arbetsuppgifter Som postdoktor förväntas du: Planera och genomföra den finländska Society Quest-processen i nära samarbete med forskargrupperna vid Hanken och Linköpings universitet samt stödja genomförandet i Sverige. Kartlägga och engagera relevanta intressenter inom näringsliv, myndigheter, transportinfrastruktur och forskarsamhället. Rekrytera deltagare till Society Quest och koordinera intressenternas medverkan. Bidra till utformning och facilitering av samskapande workshoppar kring resilienta och miljömässigt hållbara godstransporter. Systematiskt dokumentera och analysera resultat tillsammans med projektets forskare. Bidra till projektets kommunikation och spridning av resultat. Förbereda vetenskapliga artiklar baserade på projektets resultat. Utföra undervisningsuppgifter motsvarande högst 15 % av arbetstiden. Kvalifikationer Den framgångsrika kandidaten förväntas ha: Doktorsexamen inom supply chain management, logistik, transporter, hållbarhet eller annat relevant område. Kunskap om, eller ett starkt forskningsintresse för, försörjningskedjors resiliens, hållbara transporter, godstransporter eller närliggande områden. Erfarenhet av kvalitativa och/eller deltagande forskningsmetoder, exempelvis intervjuer, workshoppar, fokusgrupper, samskapande processer eller intressentbaserad forskning. Förmåga att självständigt organisera och genomföra empirisk forskning, inklusive identifiering och rekrytering av intressenter, datainsamling, dokumentation och analys. God förmåga att samarbeta och kommunicera med såväl akademiska som icke-akademiska aktörer. Utmärkta kunskaper i engelska, både muntligt och skriftligt. Meriterande Erfarenhet av samarbete med företag, myndigheter, infrastrukturaktörer eller andra samhällsaktörer. Erfarenhet av att leda workshoppar eller arbeta med samskapandemetoder. Kunskap om forskning kring resiliens och hållbarhet samt samspelet mellan dessa områden. Kunskaper i finska och/eller svenska. Kvalificerade vetenskapliga publikationer. Undervisningserfarenhet. Erfarenhet från näringslivet. Du får möjlighet att Bidra till ett nordiskt forskningsprojekt och påverka dess genomförande. Utveckla expertis inom resilienta och hållbara godstransporter. Bygga nätverk med forskare, företag och offentliga aktörer i Finland och Sverige. Få erfarenhet av samskapande, intressentengagemang och gränsöverskridande forskning. Bidra till vetenskapliga publikationer, samhällsnytta och utveckling av framtida forskning. Skaffa akademisk undervisningserfarenhet. Behörighetskrav Sökande ska: Ha avlagt doktorsexamen inom ett relevant ämne. Behärska engelska flytande. Även sökande som ännu inte har disputerat kan beaktas om disputationsdatum redan har fastställts. Tillträde ska kunna ske senast i februari 2027. Om anställningen Tjänsten är tidsbegränsad till 8 månader , beroende på när du kan börja (tidigaste start januari 2027). Genom att ansluta dig till ämnesområdet Supply Chain Management & Social Responsibility vid Hanken blir du en del av en dynamisk vetenskaplig miljö vid en handelshögskola med så kallad Triple Crown -ackreditering (AACSB, EQUIS och AMBA). Du kommer att arbeta i en grupp av mycket aktiva forskare med hög publiceringstakt, omfattande internationella projekt och en stark internationell profil. Den årliga arbetstiden är 1 612 timmar . Arbetsorten är Helsingfors , och vi förutsätter att du flyttar till Finland. Lön och förmåner Lönen för projektforskaren följer det finländska universitetens lönesystem och omfattar företagshälsovård samt pensions- och semesterförmåner. Ingångslönen ligger inom intervallet 46 800–52 500 euro per år , beroende på den valda kandidatens kvalifikationer och prestationer. Ansökningshandlingar Ansökan ska innehålla: Motivationsbrev med beskrivning av hur du skulle bidra till projektet. CV inklusive minst två referenser som kan kontaktas. Examensbevis för doktorsexamen. Publikationsförteckning inklusive fungerande DOI-länkar till max fem utvalda, nyligen publicerade arbeten (alternativt publikationerna som separata PDF-filer om länkarna inte fungerar). Ytterligare relevanta dokument, såsom intyg och rekommendationer, kan bifogas. Ansökan Ansökan ska lämnas in elektroniskt via Hankens rekryteringssystem Laura senast 16 november 2026 . Ange även när du kan tillträda tjänsten om du blir vald. Kontaktpersoner Biträdande professor Anna Aminoff – anna.aminoff@hanken.fi Biträdande professor Helleke Heikkinen – helleke.heikkinen@hanken.fi Övrigt Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan förbehåller sig rätten att, av motiverade skäl, lämna tjänsten obesatt, förlänga ansökningstiden eller beakta kandidater som inte lämnat in ansökan under den ordinarie ansökningsperioden. Hanken förbehåller sig även rätten att avsluta rekryteringen tidigare om en lämplig kandidat identifieras och anställs. Mer information HUMLOG Institute: http://www.hanken.fi/humloginstitute Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan: https://www.hanken.fi/ Application period starts: 2026-10-22 15:00 Application period ends: 2026-11-16 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=406&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=407&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=1zgkynaa3tmso0ogsskg84kckswgkok": {
      "title": "The position",
      "description": "Biträdande professor (nivå 1 eller 2, tenure track) i nationalekonomi / Assistant or Associate Professor (Tenure Track) in Economics We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Biträdande professor (nivå 1 eller 2, tenure track) i nationalekonomi / Assistant or Associate Professor (Tenure Track) in Economics (For English, see below) Svenska handelshögskolan (Hanken) ledigförklarar en befattning som biträdande professor (nivå 1 eller 2, tenure track) i nationalekonomi med tillträde senast i september 2027 eller enligt överenskommelse. Befattningen är placerad vid ämnet nationalekonomi i Helsingfors. Befattningen Sökande inom samtliga områden av nationalekonomi kommer att beaktas för anställningen som biträdande professor (nivå 1 eller 2). Viss preferens ges till sökande med inriktning på politisk ekonomi i bred bemärkelse. Undervisning på svenska förutsätts. Befattningen ingår i Hankens forskningsorienterade karriärstig (tenure track) och är öppen för personer med potential för en framstående vetenskaplig karriär. Den som anställs har möjlighet att avancera genom utvärdering av meriter inom alla relevanta områden i enlighet med Hankens tenure track riktlinjer . En anställning som biträdande professor (nivå 1) är tidsbunden för 5 år med möjlighet om att anhålla om en förlängning på 2 år. Befordran till biträdande professor (nivå 2) förutsätter en utvärdering i enlighet med Hankens tenure track riktlinjer. En anställning som biträdande professor (nivå 2) är tillsvidare. Nationalekonomi vid Hanken Hanken är en forskningsinriktad handelshögskola som erbjuder utbildning på svenska och engelska. Ämnet nationalekonomi bedriver högklassig undervisning och forskning, med särskilda styrkeområden inom industriell organisation, beteende- och experimentell ekonomi, arbetsmarknadsekonomi, samt empirisk och teoretisk mikroekonomi i bredare bemärkelse. Vi erbjuder heltäckande utbildning på kandidat-, magister- och doktorandnivå. Helsinki Graduate School of Economics Ämnet nationalekonomi vid Hanken är en aktiv partner i Helsinki Graduate School of Economics (Helsinki GSE). Helsinki GSE sammanför nationalekonomer från tre finländska universitet: Aalto-universitetet, Svenska handelshögskolan och Helsingfors universitet. Dess uppdrag är att bedriva framstående forskning med största möjliga akademiska och samhälleliga genomslag, utbilda nästa generation ekonomer på internationell toppnivå och erbjuda högklassig utbildning över ämnesgränserna. Helsinki GSE samarbetar nära med Statens ekonomiska forskningscentral VATT (https://www.vatt.fi/en/). Helsinki GSE erbjuder en mångsidig och aktiv forskningsmiljö med elva forskningsgrupper inom olika områden av nationalekonomi. Undervisningen inom Helsinki GSE samordnas mellan partneruniversiteten för att maximera genomslaget för studenterna och samhället. Hanken och Helsinki GSE är centralt belägna i Helsingfors. Här hittar du mera information om ämnet nationalekonomi och Helsinki GSE . Behörighetskrav Sökande bedöms utifrån forskning, undervisning, aktivitet inom den vetenskapliga gemenskapen och samhällelig påverkan. Den som söker anställning som biträdande professor (nivå 1) ska ha doktorsexamen i nationalekonomi eller ett närliggande område, eller vara nära att slutföra sin doktorsexamen. Särskild vikt läggs vid den sökandes potential att bedriva högklassig vetenskaplig forskning och ge högklassig undervisning i nationalekonomi. Utöver de krav som ställs på en biträdande professor (nivå 1), ska sökande till biträdande professor (nivå 2) ha uppnått och kunnat uppvisa internationellt hög nivå på sin forskning inom positionens vetenskapsområde, hög nivå i undervisningen och bidragit med att delta i gemensamma uppdrag vid universitet ( institutional service ) samt främjat samhällelig växelverkan. Som fristående handelshögskola med starka nordiska rötter erbjuder Hanken högklassiga examensprogram på svenska och engelska. Av sökande krävs flytande kunskaper i både engelska och svenska. Undervisning på svenska ingår i arbetsuppgifterna. Akademisk personal vid Hanken förväntas bedriva och handleda vetenskaplig forskning, ge högklassig akademisk undervisning, följa utvecklingen inom sitt område samt bidra till Hanken, den akademiska gemenskapen och samhället. Undervisningsuppgifterna fördelas utifrån ämnets behov i undervisningsplanen och den anställdas relevanta kompetens. Anställningen är på heltid och den årliga arbetstiden är 1612 timmar. Under läsåret förväntas den anställda vara anträffbar på institutionen i Helsingfors i genomsnitt minst tre dagar per vecka för att aktivt bidra till forsknings- och undervisningsmiljön. Hanken förutsätter att akademiska medarbetare bor och arbetar i Finland och erbjuder flyttstöd till personer som rekryteras från utlandet. Lön Lönen fastställs enligt lönesystemet för universiteten i Finland (företagshälsovård och pensions- och semesterpremier ingår i anställningen). Den exakta lönenivån beror på den anställdas kvalifikationer. Hanken stöder den valda kandidaten med en startbudget för forskning. Det är dessutom möjligt att ansöka om ytterligare anslag för forskning, resor och utveckling av undervisningen. Hanken belönar excellens inom både forskning och undervisning. Tilläggsinformation För ytterligare information, kontakta professor Topi Miettinen, topi.miettinen@hanken.fi . Allmänna anvisningar för sökande finns här . Mer information om Hanken som arbetsgivare finns här . Rekryteringsprocess och tidsplan Ansökningstiden går ut den 17 november 2026 . Intervjuer genomförs online efter ansökningstidens utgång inom ramen för European Job Market Online Interview Window den 14–17 december 2026. De kandidater som går vidare bjuds in till ett campusbesök som omfattar en intervju och en forskningspresentation. Hur ansöker man Ansökan ska riktas till rektor och innehålla följande handlingar: Ansökan där den sökande specificerar vilken position hen söker (biträdande professor, nivå 1 eller nivå 2) Meritförteckning (CV) inklusive publikationslista. Ett standardiserat Job Market-CV inom nationalekonomi är tillräckligt. En ofta använd CV-mall finns här . Ansökningsbrev som innehåller beskrivning av tidigare forskning, dess vetenskapliga kvalitet och akademiska påverkan, planer för framtida forskning och sökandes deltagande i gemensamma uppdrag (eng. institutional service ) vid den egna institutionen och universitetet samt kandidatens samhälleliga växelverkan. För sökande till biträdande professor (nivå 2) ska ansökningsbrevet även innehålla beskrivning av forskningssamarbete med andra forskare, kontribution till internationella vetenskapliga nätverk, engagemang i ansökningar om extern forskningsfinansiering och kontribution till den pedagogiska utvecklingen inom institutionen eller universitetet utöver den egna undervisningen. Ansökan ska vara skriven med den öppna positionen i åtanke. Kopior av fem forskningspublikationer som bäst demonstrerar forskning av hög vetenskaplig kvalitet. En undervisningsportfölj (för exempel på innehåll, se här ) Tre referensbrev från akademiska forskare. Breven lämnas in via EconJobMarket eller skickas direkt till Hanken på humanresources@hanken.fi . Samtliga ansökningshandlingar ska lämnas in på engelska via rekryteringsdatabasen LAURA. Ansökningstiden går ut den 17 november 2026. Om Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan, Hanken, placerar sig bland de ledande handelshögskolorna i Norden. Hanken finns i Finland med kampus i Helsingfors och Vasa. Hanken erbjuder program på kandidat-, magister- och doktorandnivå samt EMBA och Executive Development -program som går på svenska eller engelska.  Hanken har 2 725 kandidat- och magisterstuderande samt 118 doktorander. Universitetet har nära kontakt med näringslivet och ett aktivt alumnnätverk med över 13 800 alumner i mer än 70 länder. Hanken har de tre mest ansedda ackrediteringarna; AACSB, AMBA och EQUIS. Hanken finns rankad i Financial Times Masters in Management på plats 56 (2026). Hanken är även känt för sin högkvalitativa forskning, internationella inriktning och fokus på hållbarhet. ------------------------------- Hanken School of Economics invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor (tenure track) in Economics, with the appointment beginning no later than September 2027 (negotiable). The position is based in the Economics Unit in Helsinki. The position Candidates from all fields of economics will be considered for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor. Some preference will be given to candidates working in political economics, broadly defined. Teaching in Swedish is expected. The position is part of Hanken’s research-oriented tenure-track system and is open to individuals with the potential for an excellent scientific career. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to advance through evaluations that consider merits in all relevant areas in accordance with Hanken’s tenure track guidelines .  The Assistant Professor position is fixed-term for 5 years, with the possibility to apply for a 2-year extension. Promotion to Associate Professor is subject to a tenure evaluation in accordance with Hanken’s tenure track guidelines. The Associate Professor position is permanent. Economics at Hanken Hanken School of Economics is a research-oriented business school offering education in English and Swedish. Hanken’s Economics Unit is committed to high-quality teaching and research, with strengths in industrial organisation, behavioural and experimental economics, labour economics and empirical and theoretical microeconomics more broadly. We offer comprehensive undergraduate, master’s and doctoral programmes. Helsinki Graduate School of Economics Hanken’s Economics Unit is an active partner in the Helsinki Graduate School of Economics (Helsinki GSE). Helsinki GSE brings together economics faculty from three Finnish universities: Aalto University, Hanken School of Economics and the University of Helsinki. Its mission is to produce outstanding research with maximum academic and societal impact, educate the next generation of world-class economists, and offer excellent training across disciplinary boundaries. Helsinki GSE collaborates closely with the VATT Institute for Economic Research (https://www.vatt.fi/en/). Helsinki GSE offers a versatile and active research environment and hosts eleven research groups in various fields of economics. Teaching within Helsinki GSE is coordinated among its partner universities to maximise its impact on students and society. Hanken and Helsinki GSE are conveniently located in central Helsinki. For more information, please visit the Economics unit and Helsinki GSE . Requirements Applicants will be evaluated based on their research, teaching, institutional service and societal impact.  Applicants on the assistant professor level should hold a doctoral degree, or be close to completing one, in economics or a related field. Particular emphasis will be placed on applicants’ potential to conduct high-quality scientific research and provide high-quality teaching in economics. In addition to the requirements for an assistant professor, applicants for the associate professor level are expected to have demonstrated internationally high levels of research within the scientific field of the position, high levels in teaching and contributed through institutional service and societal impact. As an independent business school with strong Nordic roots, Hanken offers high-quality degree programmes in Swedish and English. Applicants for the current position are required to have a fluent command of both English and Swedish. Teaching in Swedish is expected as part of the position's responsibilities. Academic staff at Hanken are expected to conduct and supervise scientific research, provide high-quality academic teaching, remain abreast of developments in their field, and contribute to Hanken, the academic community and society. Teaching duties are allocated based on the curriculum needs of the subject and the appointee’s relevant expertise. The full-time position has an annual working time of 1,612 hours. During the academic year, the appointee is expected to work at the office in Helsinki for an average of at least three days per week to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment. Hanken requires academic employees to reside and work in Finland and provides relocation support for applicants moving to Finland from abroad. Salary The salary is determined in accordance with the salary system for Finnish universities and includes occupational health care as well as pension and holiday benefits. The exact salary level depends on the appointee’s qualifications. Hanken provides the selected candidate with a start-up research budget. Additional grants for research, travel and teaching development may also be applied for. Hanken rewards excellence in both research and teaching. Further information For further information, please contact Professor Topi Miettinen, topi.miettinen@hanken.fi . General instructions for applicants are available here . More information about Hanken as an employer is available here . Recruitment process and timeline The application deadline is 17 November 2026 . Candidates will be interviewed online after the application deadline in the European Job Market Online Interview Window, December 14-17, 2026. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to an on-campus visit that includes an interview and a research presentation. How to apply The application should be addressed to the Rector and must include: Cover letter in which the applicant specifies the position for which they are applying (associate professor or assistant professor) A curriculum vitae, including a list of publications. A standard economics Job Market CV is sufficient. One commonly used CV format is available at here . Personal statement describing the applicant’s previous research and its scientific quality and academic impact, plans for future research, service to the department and university, and societal impact. For candidates applying for the associate professor level, the personal statement should also include a description of research collaboration with other scholars, contributions to international scientific networks, involvement in applications for external research funding, and contributions to the pedagogical development in the department or university beyond own teaching. The personal statement needs to be written with the announced position in mind. Copies of five research publications that best demonstrate high scientific quality research A teaching portfolio (proposed content here ) Three letters of reference from academic researchers, submitted through EconJobMarket or sent directly to Hanken at humanresources@hanken.fi . If you apply for an associate professor position only, letters are not required but recommended. Please submit all application materials in English through Hanken’s recruitment database LAURA. The application deadline is 17 November 2026. About Hanken Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries. It is located in Finland, with campuses in Helsinki and Vaasa. Hanken offers a range of B.Sc., M.Sc., EMBA, PhD, and Executive Development programmes taught mainly in English and Swedish. Hanken has 2 725 Bachelor and Master’s students, and 118 Doctoral researchers. The School has close ties to the business community and an active alumni network with over 13 800 alumni working in more than 70 countries. The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. The Master’s programme was ranked 56 in the Masters in Management by Financial Times in 2026. Hanken is also recognized for its research quality, its international orientation, and its focus on sustainability. Application period starts: 2026-10-23 13:00 Application period ends: 2026-11-17 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=407&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=405&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=1zgkynaa3tmso0ogsskg84kckswgkok": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (tenure-track) in Finance / Biträdande professor (nivå 1) i finansiell ekonomi (tenure track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (tenure-track) in Finance / Biträdande professor (nivå 1) i finansiell ekonomi (tenure track) We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Assistant Professor (tenure-track) in Finance / Biträdande professor (nivå 1) i finansiell ekonomi (tenure track) [Se nedan för svenska] Hanken School of Economics invites applications for an Assistant Professor (tenure-track) in Finance beginning no later than August 2027, or as otherwise agreed. The position is at the Finance Unit at the Department of Finance and Economics in Helsinki. For this position, we will consider candidates in all fields of Finance. The position is part of the Hanken tenure track system. It is open to talented individuals who have potential for an excellent scientific career. Individuals placed on the Hanken tenure track have the possibility to advance in their career through regular performance assessments, which consider their merits in all relevant qualification areas in accordance with Hanken’s tenure track guidelines . Hanken School of Economics is a research-oriented business school offering education in English and Swedish. Hanken’s Finance unit is committed to high-quality teaching and research. We offer full scale graduate and undergraduate programs. We have a strong research climate, reflected in a growing volume and range of research activities. We value high-quality, practice-oriented research, as evidenced by our publications in top-ranked journals. In addition, Hanken's Finance unit is an active partner in the Graduate School of Finance (GSF), which offers the national doctoral program in finance. GSF also organizes seminars and workshops for faculty members and doctoral students. Requirements The applicants will be reviewed based on their research, teaching, institutional service, and societal impact. Applicants should hold a doctoral degree (or be near completion of the doctorate) in Finance (or a related field). When evaluating the applicants’ qualifications, the main focus will be on the potential to conduct high-quality scientific research and the potential to provide high-quality teaching. A focus on asset pricing is considered a strong merit. Being a stand-alone business school with strong Nordic roots, Hanken offers degree programmes in Swedish and English. For this position, applicants are required to have fluent command of English, knowledge of Swedish is considered a merit. Hanken supports its faculty in learning the Swedish language, which serves as the administrative language of the business school. Academic staff at Hanken are expected to carry out and supervise scientific research, provide academic teaching, closely follow the advances of their field, and contribute service to Hanken, the academic community, and society.  Teaching tasks are allocated based on the curriculum needs of the subject and by considering relevant expertise. The full-time position has an annual working time of 1612 hours. During the academic year, it is expected that a minimum average of three days per week is spent at the office in Helsinki to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment. Hanken requires academic employees to reside and work in Finland, and it offers relocation support for applicants coming from outside Finland. Salary The salary is based on the university salary system in Finland (includes employee healthcare as well as pension and holiday contributions). The exact salary level depends on the recruited individual’s qualifications. Hanken will support the selected employee with a start-up research budget, and additional research, travel and teaching development grants can also be applied for. Hanken rewards excellence in both research and teaching. For more Information For additional information, please contact Head of Department Jesper Haga ( jesper.haga@hanken.fi) or Head of Subject Karl Felixson ( karl.felixson@hanken.fi) . General instructions for applicants are provided here . Also, read more about Hanken as an employer here . Recruitment process and timeline The application deadline is 22 November 2026 . Selected candidates will be interviewed online shortly after the application deadline. Short-listed candidates will be invited to on-site campus visits including an interview and research presentation. How to apply The application is to be addressed to the Rector and application materials should include: CV (proposed content here ), including list of publications. Personal statement, which includes a description of past research and its scientific quality, academic impact, plans for future research and a description of the candidate’s service to the department and university and a description of the candidate’s societal impact. Teaching portfolio (proposed content here ). Copies of no more than five research publications, including a ‘job market’ paper Three letters of reference from academic researchers, to be submitted via Econjobmarket or directly to Hanken via humanresources@hanken.fi . Please submit all application materials in English in Hanken’s recruitment database LAURA. The application deadline is 22 November 2026 . Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries. It is located in Finland, with campuses in Helsinki and Vaasa. Hanken offers a range of B.Sc., M.Sc., EMBA, PhD, and Executive Development programmes taught mainly in English and Swedish. Hanken has 2 725 Bachelor and Master’s students, and 118 Doctoral students. The School has close ties to the business community and an active alumni network with over 13 800 alumni working in more than 70 countries. The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. The Master’s programme was ranked 56 in the Masters in Management by Financial Times in 2026. Hanken is also recognized for its research quality, its international orientation, and its focus on sustainability. ---------------- Svenska handelshögskolan (Hanken) söker en biträdande professor (nivå 1) i finansiell ekonomi (tenure track) med start senast i augusti 2027 eller enligt överenskommelse. Befattningen är placerad vid ämnet finansiell ekonomi inom Institutionen för finansiell ekonomi och nationalekonomi i Helsingfors. För denna befattning beaktar vi kandidater inom alla områden av finansiell ekonomi. Befattningen ingår i Hankens forskningsorienterade karriärstig (tenure track). Den är öppen för kvalificerade kandidater med potential för en framstående vetenskaplig karriär. Kandidater som anställs inom Hankens tenure track-system har möjlighet till avancemang inom systemet genom utvärdering av meriter och prestationer inom alla relevanta områden i enlighet med Hankens riktlinjer . Svenska handelshögskolan är en forskningsinriktad handelshögskola som erbjuder utbildning på engelska och svenska.  Ämnet finansiell ekonomi vid Hanken är engagerat i högkvalitativ undervisning och forskning. Vi erbjuder program på både kandidat- och magisternivå. Vi har en stark forskningsmiljö, vilket återspeglas i en växande omfattning och bredd av forskningsverksamheten. Vi värdesätter högkvalitativ, praktiskt orienterad forskning, vilket framgår av våra publikationer i ledande vetenskapliga tidskrifter. Dessutom är ämnet finansiell ekonomi vid Hanken en aktiv partner i Graduate School of Finance (GSF), som erbjuder det nationella doktorandprogrammet i finansiell ekonomi. GSF arrangerar även seminarier och workshops för undervisande och forskande personal samt doktorander. Behörighetskrav Sökande bedöms utifrån forskning, undervisning, aktivitet inom den vetenskapliga gemenskapen och samhällelig påverkan. Sökande ska ha doktorsexamen i finansiell ekonomi (eller närliggande område) eller vara i slutskedet av sina doktorandstudier. Vid bedömningen ligger huvudfokus på potentialen att bedriva vetenskaplig forskning av hög kvalitet samt att ge undervisning av hög kvalitet. Specialisering inom tillgångsprissättning (asset pricing) betraktas som en stark merit. Som en fristående handelshögskola med stark nordisk förankring erbjuder Hanken utbildningsprogram på svenska och engelska. För befattningen krävs flytande kunskaper i engelska. Kunskaper i svenska betraktas som en merit. Hanken stöder sin personal i att lära sig svenska, som är handelshögskolans administrativa språk. Den akademiska personalen vid Hanken förväntas bedriva och handleda vetenskaplig forskning, ge akademisk undervisning, följa utvecklingen inom sitt ämnesområde samt delta i gemensamma uppdrag vid Hanken, den akademiska gemenskapen och samhället. Undervisningsuppgifter fördelas enligt undervisningsbehovet i ämnet samt den undervisande personalens expertis. Anställningen är på heltid och den årliga arbetstiden är 1612 timmar.  Under läsåret förväntar vi oss att du är anträffbar på institutionen i Helsingfors i genomsnitt minst tre arbetsdagar i veckan för att aktivt bidra till forsknings- och undervisningsmiljön. Hanken förutsätter att akademisk personal är bosatt och arbetar i Finland och erbjuder flyttstöd till personer som rekryteras från utlandet. Lön Lönen baserar sig på lönesystemet för universiteten i Finland (företagshälsovård och pensions- och semesterpremier ingår i anställningen). Den exakta lönenivån beror på den anställdas kvalifikationer. Hanken stöder nyanställd akademisk personal med en individuell startbudget för forskningen. Det finns möjlighet att ansöka om ytterligare forsknings-, rese- och undervisningsutvecklingsanslag. Hanken belönar excellens inom både forskning och undervisning. Tilläggsinformation För ytterligare information, vänligen kontakta prefekt Jesper Haga ( jesper.haga@hanken.fi ) eller ämnesansvarig Karl Felixson ( karl.felixson@hanken.fi ). Allmänna anvisningar till sökande hittar du här . Du kan också läsa mer om Hanken som arbetsgivare här . Rekryteringsprocess och tidtabell Sista ansökningsdag är den 22 november 2026. Utvalda kandidater intervjuas online kort efter ansökningstidens utgång. Kortlistade kandidater bjuds in till ett campusbesök som inkluderar en intervju samt en forskningspresentation. Ansökan Ansökan ska riktas till rektor och innehålla: CV (för exempel på innehåll, se här ), inklusive en publikationslista. Ansökningsbrev som inkluderar en beskrivning av tidigare forskning och dess vetenskapliga kvalitet, akademisk påverkan, planer för framtida forskning, en beskrivning av den sökandes deltagande i gemensamma uppdrag vid den egna institutionen och universitetet samt en beskrivning av kandidatens samhälleliga växelverkan. En undervisningsportfölj (för exempel på innehåll, se här ). Kopior av högst fem forskningspublikationer inklusive ett ”arbetsmarknadspapper” (eng. job market paper) Tre referensbrev från akademiska forskare som skickas via Econjobmarket eller direkt till Hanken via humanresources@hanken.fi . Samtliga ansökningshandlingar ska lämnas in på engelska via Hankens rekryteringssystem LAURA. Sista ansökningsdag är den 22 november 2026. Svenska handelshögskolan, Hanken, placerar sig bland de ledande handelshögskolorna i Norden. Hanken finns i Finland med kampus i Helsingfors och Vasa. Hanken erbjuder program på kandidat-, magister- och doktorandnivå samt EMBA och Executive Development -program som går på svenska eller engelska.  Hanken har 2 725 kandidat- och magisterstuderande samt 118 doktorander. Universitetet har nära kontakt med näringslivet och ett aktivt alumnnätverk med över 13 800 alumner i mer än 70 länder. Hanken har de tre mest ansedda ackrediteringarna; AACSB, AMBA och EQUIS. Hanken finns rankad i Financial Times Masters in Management på plats 56 (2026). Hanken är även känt för sin högkvalitativa forskning, internationella inriktning och fokus på hållbarhet. Application period starts: 2026-10-19 08:00 Application period ends: 2026-11-22 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=405&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=397&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=1zgkynaa3tmso0ogsskg84kckswgkok": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Management & Organisation / Biträdande professor (tenure track, nivå 1) i företagsledning och organisation",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Management & Organisation / Biträdande professor (tenure track, nivå 1) i företagsledning och organisation We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Management & Organisation / Biträdande professor (tenure track, nivå 1) i företagsledning och organisation The Department of Management and Organization at Hanken School of Economics invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Management & Organization The position is in Helsinki, starting August 1, 2027, or as agreed. Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries, and recognized for its international orientation and outstanding research quality The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. We have close ties to the business community and an active alumni network. Our master's programme is ranked 56 in the Masters in Management 2026 by Financial Times. We are located in Helsinki and Vaasa. Finland is ranked as one of the best-governed countries in the world (Legatum prosperity index, 2023), as well as the happiest country in the world (World Happiness Report 2026). The city of Helsinki ranks as one of the most liveable cities in the world (The Economist 2024). These are thanks to, among others, the high level of equality and safety; free, high-quality education at both primary, secondary, and university levels; affordable healthcare and childcare; and competitiveness and innovativeness of the business sector. The Department of Management & Organization nurtures a strong community of researchers and teachers. We have a strong research climate, reflected in the volume and diversity of research activities, including externally funded projects, publications in highly ranked academic journals, an active community of PhD researchers, and a wide range of societal impact activities. Our goal is to conduct high-quality academic research with corporate and societal relevance. The focus of our research is broad and includes areas such as organizational behaviour, people management/HRM, strategy and strategic management, AI and technology, responsibility and sustainability, and more. Our scholars engage in active collaboration with other universities and business schools around the world. Scholars associated with the subject regularly publish articles in leading international academic journals such as the Journal of Management, Organization Studies, Academy of Management Review, Strategic Management Journal, Journal of International Business Studies, Journal of Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, Human Relations and Journal of Business Ethics . Our diversity is also reflected in our courses and programme at Bachelor, Master and PhD level. The teaching covers issues within organizational behavior, HRM, strategic management, international business, social responsibility and sustainability, and business ethics. At Hanken, our goal is to educate responsible professionals for the global economy and changing society. We embrace Hanken values in teaching and learning, such as openness, equality, and integrity, and promote an innovative learning community that answers to the challenges of the global world, and that efficiently integrates students, faculty, staff, the corporate world, as well as partner organizations and universities. More information about our teaching and research can be found here: https://www.hanken.fi/en/departments-centres/department-management-and-organisation Requirements Applicants must have a doctoral degree (or be very near completion of the doctorate). The degree can be from any relevant discipline provided that the candidate’s research focus is related to the area of management and organization. A focus on organizational behavior or HRM is considered a merit. Candidates will be reviewed based on their research, teaching, institutional service, and societal impact. The main focus will be on the potential to conduct high-quality scientific research, , and the potential to provide high-quality teaching. Research is the most important of the qualification areas followed by teaching, and then, service and societal impact. Applicants for the current position are required to have a fluent command of both English and Swedish. Teaching in Swedish is expected as part of the position's responsibilities. Academic staff at Hanken are expected to carry out and supervise scientific research projects, obtain external funding, provide high-quality academic teaching, closely follow the advances of their field, and participate in service to Hanken, the larger academic community, and society. The full-time position has an annual working time of 1612 hours. During the academic year, it is expected that a minimum average of three days per week is spent at the office in Helsinki to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment, as well as to the collegial community. Hanken offers relocation support for tenure track professors coming outside Finland and expects full-time academic employees to reside and work in Finland. Teaching tasks are allocated based on the curriculum needs of the subject and by considering relevant expertise. Hanken offers multiple pedagogical training opportunities as well as Swedish language training. Salary and other benefits The salary is based on the university salary system in Finland. The exact salary level depends on qualifications and performance. At the assistant professor level, the annual salary range starts from around 60.000 euros (including a holiday bonus). In addition, the employment includes occupational healthcare as well as pension contributions. Hanken will support the appointed person with a research budget and additional rewards for excellence in research and teaching. Research, travel, and teaching development grants can also be applied for. Individuals placed on the Hanken tenure track have the possibility to advance in their career through regular performance assessments, which take into account their merits in all relevant qualification areas of the tenure track system. Interviews Short-listed candidates will be invited to on-site campus visits including an interview and research presentation. Other arrangements are possible for short-listed candidates not based in Europe. For more information For additional information, please contact Professor Mats Ehrnrooth, Head of Department, mats.ehrnrooth@hanken.fi How to apply The application is to be addressed to the Rector and application materials should include: Cover letter CV, including a list of publications (proposed content here ) Personal statement, which includes a description of past research and its scientific quality, academic impact, plans for future research, a description of the candidate’s service to the department and university, and a description of the candidate’s societal impact Copies of no more than five research publications, including a ‘job market’ paper which is an original piece of research by the candidate that constitutes their best research to date Portfolio (e.g., Teaching portfolio template ) Three letters of reference from academic researchers to be submitted directly to Hanken via humanresources@hanken.fi Relevant certificates (degree certificates, language certificates) Please submit all application materials in English. Please note that only applications submitted through the database will be considered. Full applications should be submitted through the link below no later than November 30, 2026 . General instructions for applicants are provided here . Also, read more about Hanken as an employer here . ******** Institutionen för företagsledning och organisation söker en Biträdande professor (tenure track, nivå 1) i företagsledning och organisation Befattningen är placerad i Helsingfors och anställningen börjar 1.8.2027 eller enligt överenskommelse. Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan är en av de ledande handelshögskolorna i Norden, och är erkänd för sin internationella orientering och framstående forskningskvalitet i förhållande till sin storlek. Högskolan är ackrediterad av AACSB, AMBA och EQUIS. Vi har nära band till näringslivet och ett aktivt alumninätverk. Vårt magisterprogram rankas på plats 56 i Financial Times ranking Masters in Management 2026. Vi finns i Helsingfors och Vasa. Finland rankas som ett av de bäst styrda länderna i världen (Legatum Prosperity Index, 2023), samt som världens lyckligaste land (World Happiness Report 2026). Helsingfors rankas som en av världens mest levnadsvänliga städer (The Economist 2024). Detta tack vare bland annat den höga nivån av jämställdhet och trygghet; gratis utbildning av hög kvalitet på både grundskole-, gymnasie- och universitetsnivå; prisvärd hälso- och sjukvård samt barnomsorg; samt näringslivets konkurrenskraft och innovationsförmåga. Institutionen för företagsledning och organisation har en stark gemenskap av forskare och lärare vars forskningsaktiviteter har ett brett fokus som omfattar områden som organisationsbeteende, personalledning/HRM, strategi och strategisk ledning, AI och teknologi, företagsansvar och hållbarhet, med mera. Vi har ett starkt forskningsfokus som återspeglas i en ökande volym och mångfald av forskningsaktiviteter, inklusive externt finansierade projekt, publikationer i högt rankade akademiska tidskrifter, en aktiv gemenskap av doktorander, och olika aktiviteter med social och samhällelig relevans. Våra forskare publicerar regelbundet sin forskning i ledande internationella akademiska tidskrifter som Journal of Management, Organization Studies, Strategic Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Journal of International Business Studies, Journal of Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, Human Relations och Journal of Business Ethics . Vår mångfald återspeglas också i våra kurser och program på kandidat-, magister-, och doktorandnivå. Vår undervisning präglas av variation och täcker frågor inom personaladministration och HRM samt strategi och strategisk ledning, internationellt företagande, ansvar, hållbarhet och företagsetik. Vid Hanken är vårt mål att utbilda ansvarsfulla yrkesutövare för den globala ekonomin och det föränderliga samhället. Vi omfamnar Hanken värderingar i undervisning och lärande, såsom öppenhet, jämlikhet och integritet, och främjar en mångsidig och innovativ lärandegemenskap som svarar på globala utmaningar och som effektivt integrerar studenter, fakultet, personal, näringslivet samt samarbetsorganisationer och universitet. Mer information om forskningen och undervisningen inom ämnet företagsledning finns på: https://www.hanken.fi/sv/institutioner-center/institutionen-foretagsledning-och-organisation Krav Sökande måste ha en doktorsexamen (eller bevisligen vara i slutskedet av sina doktorandstudier). Doktorsexamen kan vara från olika akademiska discipliner förutsatt att kandidatens forskningsfokus är relaterat till området företagsledning och organisation. Ett fokus på organisationsbeteende eller HRM är meriterande. Sökande kommer att granskas baserat på deras forskning, undervisning, institutionstjänstgöring och samhällspåverkan. Huvudfokus ligger på potentialen att bedriva högkvalitativ vetenskaplig forskning och på potentialen att tillhandahålla högkvalitativ undervisning. Forskning är det viktigaste av behörighetsområdena följt av undervisning och sedan gemensamma uppdrag vid universitetet samt samhällelig växelverkan. Sökande förväntas ha flytande kunskaper i både engelska och svenska. Undervisning på svenska förväntas inom ramen för tjänsten. Akademisk personal vid Hanken förväntas bedriva och handleda vetenskaplig forskning, erhålla extern finansiering, tillhandahålla högkvalitativ akademisk undervisning, noggrant följa utvecklingen inom sitt område och bidra till Hanken, den akademiska gemenskapen och samhället. Heltidsbefattningen har en årlig arbetstid på 1612 timmar. Under läsåret förväntar vi oss att du är anträffbar på institutionen i Helsingfors minst tre arbetsdagar i veckan för att aktivt bidra till forsknings- och undervisningsmiljön, samt till arbetsgemenskapen på institutionen. Hanken erbjuder flyttstöd åt forskardoktorer (tenure track) som kommer från länder utanför Finland och förväntar sig att heltidsanställd akademisk personal bor och arbetar i Finland. Undervisningsuppgifter tilldelas utgående från ämnets behov och lärarens expertis. Hanken erbjuder flera pedagogiska utbildningsmöjligheter samt utbildning i svenska språket. Lön och förmåner Lönen baserar sig på lönesystemet för universiteten i Finland. Den exakta lönenivån beror på kvalifikationer och prestationsnivå. På forskardoktornivå är årslönens utgångsnivå cirka 60 000 euro (inklusive semesterpremie). Hanken stöder forskardoktorn med en budget för forskningen. Man kan ansöka om ytterligare forsknings-, rese- och undervisningsutvecklingsanslag. Dessutom ingår företagshälsovård och pensionspremier i anställningen. Hanken belönar excellens inom forskning och undervisning. Personer som anställs på Hankens tenure track har möjlighet att främja sin karriär genom regelbundna prestationsbedömningar som beaktar deras meriter inom alla relevanta kvalifikationsområden i tenure track-systemet Intervjuer Utvalda kandidater kommer att bjudas in till besök på campus som innefattar en intervju och en forskningspresentation. Andra arrangemang kan ordnas för valda kandidater som inte är bosatta i Europa. Tilläggsinformation För ytterligare information, vänligen kontakta professor Mats Ehrnrooth, Prefekt , mats.ehrnrooth@hanken.fi . Hur ansöka Ansökningar riktas till Hankens rektor och ansökningshandlingar ska inkludera följande dokument: Ansökningsbrev CV inklusive en publikationslista (förslag till uppställning här ) Personlig redogörelse som beskriver tidigare forskning och dess vetenskapliga kvalitet, akademiskt inflytande, planer för kommande forskning, en redogörelse över den sökandes aktivitet inom institutionen och den vetenskapliga gemenskapen samt en redogörelse för den sökandes samhälleliga påverkan Max 5 forskningspublikationer, inklusive ett s.k. ’job market paper’ som utgörs av kandidatens mest framstående originalforskning/primärforskning hittills Undervisningsportfölj (t.ex. Teaching portfolio -model ) Tre rekommendationsbrev av akademiska forskare skall skickas in direkt till Hanken via humanresources@hanken.fi Relevanta diplom och intyg (examensintyg, språkintyg) Vänligen lämna in ansökningshandlingarna på engelska. Observera att endast ansökningar inlämnade via rekryteringsdatabasen beaktas. Sista ansökningsdagen är den 30 november 2026. Allmänna instruktioner för sökande finns här . Läs också mer om Hanken som arbetsgivare här . Application period starts: 2026-09-15 16:30 Application period ends: 2026-11-30 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=397&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=398&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=lqs5z4g4q4gws80wg488swoswwcg0w4": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms at Work We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms at Work [Se nedan för svenska] MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms at Work Position details Recruiting institution: Hanken School of Economics, Department of Management and Organisation Work location: Helsinki, Finland · one position Contract: four-year, full-time doctoral scholarship · 48 months Expected start: 1 February 2027 or by agreement Application deadline: by 11:59 p.m. on 29 October 2026 Doctoral programme: PhD in Management and Organisation Apply: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?o=A_LOJ&list=1&lang=en&rspvt=bx32qk756igw8ww08c0k4sgg0w8w48c Hanken School of Economics, Department of Management and Organisation invites applications for this four-year doctoral scholarship in the EMANAIRE project, PhD project: “AI-Mediated Communication and Collaboration Norms at Work”. About EMANAIRE EMANAIRE is a Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Network bringing together 15 doctoral candidates at nine European universities to study how AI is changing work. Its projects examine what happens when generative and agentic AI enters leadership, everyday workflows, team communication, professional learning and career decisions. Across the network, human agency means the practical ability to understand AI-supported decisions, exercise judgement, question outputs and shape how work is organised. Each researcher joins an international cohort, receives supervision across institutions and takes part in three residential schools, methods workshops, monthly research seminars and joint work with organisations beyond academia. Every project includes extensive engagement with industrial partner (e.g. in terms of data collection and development of practice). The doctoral project As AI becomes embedded in everyday work, employees increasingly interact with AI agents, but also encounter AI-mediated contributions from colleagues. Messages may be written, filtered or delivered with AI, while autonomous agents increasingly participate in work processes and collaboration. This doctoral project examines how these developments shape relational aspects of work, (which may include authenticity, trust, social connection, and experiences of loneliness), as people negotiate emerging norms around AI use, disclosure, and appropriate forms of interaction. Through ethnographic research in AI-intensive settings, you will follow relational practices as they evolve over time and identify the mechanisms behind change. The project will develop evidence-based guidance that supports transparency, social connection and responsible AI use in organisational life. Practitioner outputs include AI- aware communication norms, guidance on disclosure and authenticity in AI-assisted exchanges, and leadership practices that protect social connection and prevent relational deterioration. In addition, the doctoral project is expected to advance scientific knowledge in relation to the doctoral topic. Your work Examine how interactions among people, AI agents and AI-mediated communication shape workplace relationships and collaboration. Conduct ethnographic research on how employees make sense of and negotiate AI use in workplace interactions, including norms of disclosure and transparency, and how these processes shape relational aspects of work. Identify the mechanisms through which AI-mediated contributions and autonomous agents reshape relational dynamics, and develop evidence-based guidance for responsible and socially sustainable AI use. Develop AI-aware communication norms and leadership guidance that protect social connection at work. Refine the research questions and design with the supervision team and prepare ethics, data-management and open-science materials. Complete a doctoral thesis and related research outputs under the host doctoral programme and EMANAIRE plan. Take part in local and network-wide training, cohort activities, reviews, dissemination and practitioner engagement. Participate in teaching related activities at the Department of Management and Organisation. Undertake collaboration with the industry partner and a separate academic mobility visit. Contribute to research integrity, equality, responsible AI, open science and FAIR data practices. Supervision, training and mobility Project contact: Emma Nordbäck ( emma.nordback@hanken.fi ). Main supervisor: Associate Professor Emma Nordbäck (Hanken School of Economics). Current DoA plan: The Doctoral researcher is expected to spend a period of time at an industrial partner conducting the ethnographic research and contributing to practice. Academic mobility visit: At least three months at another partner institution of the EMANAIRE network. The researcher will complete at least 60 ECTS of doctoral coursework, including at least 10 ECTS through network-wide provision. EMANAIRE combines local doctoral courses with three residential schools, monthly paper-development seminars, work-package workshops and network reviews. A Personal Career Development Plan will be agreed within the first three months and reviewed every six months. About Hanken School of Economics Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries. It is located in Finland, with campuses in Helsinki and Vaasa. Hanken offers a range of B.Sc., M.Sc., EMBA, PhD, and Executive Development programmes taught mainly in English and Swedish. The School has close ties to the business community and an active alumni network with over 13 800 alumni working in more than 70 countries. The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. The Hanken Masters in Management programme was ranked  #56 by the Financial Times in 2026. Hanken is recognized for its research quality, its international orientation, and its focus on sustainability. Hanken is part of the European ENGAGE.EU European university alliance, that collaborates in the area of doctoral education by creating common practices and offering courses across member universities. The Department of Management and Organisation is recognized for its outstanding research in areas such as organisation studies, human resource management, business ethics and strategic entrepreneurship. The doctoral programme at Hanken is designed as a four-year full-time education, consisting of coursework, thesis work and teaching. Hanken provides comprehensive support throughout the doctoral journey, including supervision, study administration, performance monitoring, and assistance with funding. There is also support for applying for postdoctoral research funding. Who we are looking for Applicants should hold, or be close to completing by the start date, a relevant master's degree or equivalent and demonstrate the potential to undertake independent doctoral research. Research, policy or industry experience relevant to the project is advantageous. In order to be accepted as a Doctoral Researcher at Hanken, applicants must fulfill the formal admission requirements for PhD studies : https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments . A Master’s degree is required. Please ensure that all required attachments are submitted, as they are essential for the academic evaluation of your application. Only applications and attachments sent in through the recruitment system LAURA will be considered. Project-relevant experience and qualifications include: Interest in human side of AI-mediated work, including topics such as communication, collaboration, authenticity, trust, social connection and loneliness. Strong qualitative research skills, including training in ethnography, interviews, observation or longitudinal qualitative research. Ability to study emergent informal norms and relational dynamics in organisational settings, requiring close interaction with participants, strong interpersonal skills, and the capacity to build trust and maintain productive relationships over time. Excellent academic writing and communication skills in English. Employment The scholarship is currently EUR 3755 /month and will be adjusted according to applicable regulations. The salary is based on the university salary system in Finland, which includes free access to employee healthcare as well as pension and holiday bonus. The exact salary level depends on the recruited individual’s qualifications. The salary for the last year differs from the other years and will be according to Hanken’s regular PhD salary. The full-time position has an annual workload of 1,612 hours. During the academic year, we expect you to be present at the department in Helsinki at least three working days per week to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment. Supervision and integration at Hanken The selected candidate will receive close supervision and follow-up from research faculty. The main supervisor is Associate Professor Emma Nordbäck (Hanken School of Economics). In addition, the selected candidate will receive one to two co-supervisors from the EMANAIRE network. The candidate will be integrated into the Department of Management and Organisation and the wider EMANAIRE network. Further information about the doctoral programme and admission requirements is available from Hankens PhD Administration: admissions@hanken.fi How to apply The application should include: Curriculum vitae. Degree certificates and academic transcripts (including diploma supplement if applicable) or evidence that the qualifying degree will be completed before the start date. If your educational certificates are not issued in English submit an official translation to English including copies in the original language. At least two academic or professional references, following the host's stated submission procedure. A 2,000-word research proposal showing independent engagement with this doctoral project and outlining the proposed focus, methods and relevant literature. A declaration covering doctoral status and the MSCA mobility rule. Certificate of language proficiency (see Hanken’s English language requirements at https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/language-requirement/english-language-requirements) Passport copy Academic text (at least 7000 words) Aptitude test or sufficient GPA (see requirements at: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/gpa-or-gmatgre ) Statement of Purpose written on Hankens template, see: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments), Please submit all application materials in English. Submit your application electronically via Hanken’s recruitment database Laura no later than by 11:59 p.m. on October 29th, 2026 (EET) . General instructions for applicants are provided here: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments MSCA eligibility Applicants may be of any nationality. To be eligible for MSCA funding, the selected candidate must, on the first day of MSCA employment: (i) not hold a doctoral degree; candidates who have successfully defended a doctoral thesis but have not yet formally received the degree are not eligible; (ii) comply with the MSCA mobility rule, meaning they must not have resided or carried out their main activity (work, studies, etc.) in Finland for more than 12 months during the 36 months immediately preceding that date, excluding compulsory national service, short stays such as holidays, and time spent in a procedure for obtaining refugee status under the Geneva Convention; and (iii) be enrolled in, or meet the conditions required for timely enrolment in, the doctoral programme leading to the degree specified in this notice. The appointment is conditional on documentary verification of these conditions and fulfilment of the host institution's doctoral admission requirements. More information Questions about the project can be addressed to Emma Nordbäck at emma.nordback@hanken.fi . Questions about the application process can be sent to Hanken’s PhD Administration at admissions@hanken.fi --- På svenska --- MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC10: AI-medierad kommunikation och samarbetsnormer i arbetslivet Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan, Institutionen för företagsledning och organisation, inbjuder ansökningar till detta fyraåriga doktorandstipendium inom projektet EMANAIRE. Doktorandprojektet har titeln ”AI-medierad kommunikation och samarbetsnormer i arbetslivet” . Om EMANAIRE EMANAIRE är ett Marie Skłodowska-Curie Doctoral Network som samlar 15 doktorander vid nio europeiska universitet för att studera hur AI förändrar arbetslivet. Projektet undersöker vad som händer när generativ och agentisk AI blir en del av ledarskap, dagliga arbetsflöden, teamkommunikation, professionellt lärande och karriärbeslut. Inom nätverket definieras mänsklig handlingsförmåga som den praktiska förmågan att förstå AI-stödda beslut, utöva omdöme, ifrågasätta resultat och påverka hur arbete organiseras. Varje doktorand blir en del av en internationell forskningsmiljö, får handledning över institutionsgränser och deltar i internatskolor, metodworkshoppar, månatliga forskningsseminarier och samarbete med organisationer utanför akademin. Varje projekt inkluderar dessutom aktivit engagemag med industripartner. Doktorandprojektet I takt med att AI blir en integrerad del av det dagliga arbetet interagerar medarbetare allt oftare med AI-agenter och möter AI-medierade bidrag från kollegor. Meddelanden kan skrivas, filtreras eller förmedlas med hjälp av AI, samtidigt som autonoma agenter i allt större utsträckning deltar i arbetsprocesser och samarbete. Projektet undersöker hur dessa utvecklingar påverkar arbetets relationella dimensioner, såsom autenticitet, tillit, social samhörighet eller upplevelser av ensamhet, när människor förhandlar fram nya normer kring AI-användning, transparens och lämpliga interaktionsformer. Genom etnografisk forskning i AI-intensiva miljöer kommer du att följa hur relationella praktiker förändras över tid och identifiera mekanismerna bakom dessa förändringar. Projektet kommer att utveckla evidensbaserade riktlinjer som stödjer transparens, social samhörighet och ansvarsfull AI-användning i organisatoriskt liv. Praktikorienterade resultat inkluderar AI-medvetna kommunikationsnormer, riktlinjer kring transparens och autenticitet i AI-stödda interaktioner samt ledarskapspraktiker som skyddar social samhörighet och motverkar försämrade relationer. Projektet förväntas även bidra med ny vetenskaplig kunskap inom forskningsområdet. Närmare information om arbetsuppgifter, handledning, utbildning och mobilitet samt vem vi söker och anställningsvillkor hittas i den engelska versionen av annonsen. Handledning och integrering vid Hanken Den utvalda kandidaten kommer att få nära handledning och kontinuerlig uppföljning av forskande fakultetsmedlemmar. Huvudhandledare är biträdande professor Emma Nordbäck (Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan). Dessutom kommer den antagna doktoranden att tilldelas en till två bihandledare från EMANAIRE-nätverket . Doktoranden kommer att integreras i Institutionen för ledning och organisation samt i det bredare EMANAIRE-nätverket . Ytterligare information om doktorandprogrammet och antagningskraven finns via Hankens doktorandadministration: admissions@hanken.fi . Ansökan ska innehålla: Curriculum Vitae. Examensbevis och studieutdrag samt vid behov Diploma Supplement. Minst två akademiska eller professionella referenser. En forskningsplan på cirka 2 000 ord. Intyg om uppfyllande av MSCA:s mobilitetsregel. Intyg över engelska språkkunskaper. Kopia av pass. Akademisk text (minst 7 000 ord). Lämplighetstest eller tillräckligt GPA-värde. Statement of Purpose enligt Hankens mall. Samtliga ansökningshandlingar ska lämnas in på engelska. Skicka in din ansökan elektroniskt via Hankens rekryteringsdatabas Laura senast 29 oktober 2026 (EET) . MSCA-behörighet Sökande kan vara av vilken nationalitet som helst. För att vara berättigad till finansiering inom MSCA måste den utvalda kandidaten, på den första dagen av sin MSCA-anställning: Inte inneha en doktorsexamen. Kandidater som framgångsrikt har försvarat sin doktorsavhandling men ännu inte formellt tilldelats doktorsexamen är inte behöriga. Uppfylla MSCA:s mobilitetsregel, vilket innebär att kandidaten inte får ha varit bosatt eller bedrivit sin huvudsakliga verksamhet (arbete, studier etc.) i Finland under mer än 12 månader under de 36 månader som omedelbart föregår anställningens startdatum. Undantag gäller för obligatorisk nationell tjänstgöring, kortare vistelser såsom semester samt tid som tillbringats i en process för att erhålla flyktingstatus enligt Genèvekonventionen. Vara antagen till, eller uppfylla villkoren för att kunna antas inom utsatt tid till, det doktorandprogram som leder till den examen som anges i denna utlysning. Anställningen är villkorad av att dessa krav kan styrkas genom relevant dokumentation samt att värdinstitutionens krav för antagning till forskarutbildningen uppfylls. Application period starts: 2026-09-15 16:19 Application period ends: 2026-10-29 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=398&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=401&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=lqs5z4g4q4gws80wg488swoswwcg0w4": {
      "title": "Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC 06: AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries",
      "description": "Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC 06: AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Doctoral Researcher: MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC 06: AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries [Se nedan för svenska] MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC06: AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries Position details Recruiting institution: Hanken School of Economics, Department of Management and Organisation Work location: Helsinki, Finland · one position Contract: four-year, full-time doctoral scholarship · 48 months Expected start: 1 February 2027 or by agreement Application deadline: by 11:59 p.m. on 29 October 2026 Doctoral programme: PhD in Management and Organisation Apply: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?o=A_LOJ&list=1&lang=en&rspvt=bx32qk756igw8ww08c0k4sgg0w8w48c Hanken School of Economics, Department of Management and Organisation invites applications for this four-year doctoral scholarship in the EMANAIRE project, PhD project: “AI Co-Creation, Morality, and the Inner Good in Creative Industries”. About EMANAIRE EMANAIRE is a Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions Doctoral Network bringing together 15 doctoral candidates at nine European universities to study how AI is changing work. Its projects examine what happens when generative and agentic AI enters leadership, everyday workflows, team communication, professional learning and career decisions. Across the network, human agency means the practical ability to understand AI-supported decisions, exercise judgement, question outputs and shape how work is organised. Each researcher joins an international cohort, receives supervision across institutions and takes part in three residential schools, methods workshops, monthly research seminars and joint work with organisations beyond academia. Every project includes extensive engagement with industrial partner (e.g. in terms of data collection and development of practice). The doctoral project What happens to the value and purpose of creative work when people create alongside AI? This project studies how AI agents, AI-mediated processes and platform algorithms reshape co-creation and moral questions in creative industries. It follows employees, freelancers and studios as they negotiate changes to their work and business models. Through ethnographic fieldwork you will research what practitioners value within the activity of making creative work, and how that changes across human, hybrid and automated practices. The project aims to develop a practice-based account of co-creation and offer guidance for organisations and policymakers seeking equitable, responsible and sustainable creative work. Your work Study how AI agents and platform algorithms reshape co-creation, moral questions and business models in creative industries. Conduct ethnographic fieldwork with employees, freelancers and studios. Examine what practitioners value in creative work across human, hybrid and automated practices. Develop a practice-based account and guidance for equitable, responsible and sustainable creative work. Refine the research questions and design with the supervision team and prepare ethics, data-management and open-science materials. Complete a doctoral thesis and related research outputs under the host doctoral programme and EMANAIRE plan. Take part in local and network-wide training, cohort activities, reviews, dissemination and practitioner engagement. Participate in teaching related activities at the Department of Management and Organisation. Undertake collaboration with the industry partner and a separate academic mobility visit. Contribute to research integrity, equality, responsible AI, open science and FAIR data practices. Supervision, training and mobility Project contact: Mikko Vesa ( mikko.vesa@hanken.fi ). Main supervisor: Professor Mikko Vesa (Hanken School of Economics). Current DoA plan: The Doctoral researcher is expected to spend a period of time at an industrial partner conducting the ethnographic research and contributing to practice. Academic mobility visit: At least three months at another partner institution of the EMANAIRE network . The researcher will complete at least 60 ECTS of doctoral coursework, including at least 10 ECTS through network-wide provision. EMANAIRE combines local doctoral courses with three residential schools, monthly paper-development seminars, work-package workshops and network reviews. A Personal Career Development Plan will be agreed within the first three months and reviewed every six months. About Hanken School of Economics Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries. It is located in Finland, with campuses in Helsinki and Vaasa. Hanken offers a range of B.Sc., M.Sc., EMBA, PhD, and Executive Development programmes taught mainly in English and Swedish. The School has close ties to the business community and an active alumni network with over 13 800 alumni working in more than 70 countries. The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. The Hanken Masters in Management programme was ranked  #56 by the Financial Times in 2026. Hanken is recognized for its research quality, its international orientation, and its focus on sustainability. Hanken is part of the European ENGAGE.EU European university alliance, that collaborates in the area of doctoral education by creating common practices and offering courses across member universities. The Department of Management and Organisation is recognized for its outstanding research in areas such as organisation studies, human resource management, business ethics and strategic entrepreneurship. The doctoral programme at Hanken is designed as a four-year full-time education, consisting of coursework, thesis work and teaching. Hanken provides comprehensive support throughout the doctoral journey, including supervision, study administration, performance monitoring, and assistance with funding. There is also support for applying for postdoctoral research funding. Who we are looking for Applicants should hold, or be close to completing by the start date, a relevant master's degree or equivalent and demonstrate the potential to undertake independent doctoral research. Research, policy or industry experience relevant to the project is advantageous. In order to be accepted as a Doctoral Researcher at Hanken, applicants must fulfill the formal admission requirements for PhD studies : https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments . A Master’s degree is required. Please ensure that all required attachments are submitted, as they are essential for the academic evaluation of your application. Only applications and attachments sent in through the recruitment system LAURA will be considered. Project-relevant experience and qualifications include: Interest and knowledge about the creative industries, including tareas such as e.g., media, gaming, music, arts, and design. Strong qualitative research skills, including training in ethnography, interviews, observation or longitudinal qualitative research. Ability to study work practices and ethical dynamics in organisational settings, requiring close interaction with participants, strong interpersonal skills, and the capacity to build trust and maintain productive relationships over time. Excellent academic writing and communication skills in English. Employment The scholarship is currently EUR 3755 /month and will be adjusted according to applicable regulations. The salary is based on the university salary system in Finland, which includes free access to employee healthcare as well as pension and holiday bonus. The exact salary level depends on the recruited individual’s qualifications. The salary for the last year differs from the other years and will be according to Hanken’s regular PhD salary. The full-time position has an annual workload of 1,612 hours. During the academic year, we expect you to be present at the department in Helsinki at least three working days per week to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment. Supervision and integration at Hanken The selected candidate will receive close supervision and follow-up from research faculty. The main supervisor is Professor Mikko Vesa (Hanken School of Economics). In addition, the selected candidate will receive one to two co-supervisors from the EMANAIRE network. The candidate will be integrated into the Department of Management and Organisation and the wider EMANAIRE network. Further information about the doctoral programme and admission requirements is available from Hankens PhD Administration: admissions@hanken.fi . How to apply The application should include: Curriculum vitae. Degree certificates and academic transcripts (including diploma supplement if applicable) or evidence that the qualifying degree will be completed before the start date. If your educational certificates are not issued in English submit an official translation to English including copies in the original language. At least two academic or professional references, following the host's stated submission procedure. A 2,000-word research proposal showing independent engagement with this doctoral project and outlining the proposed focus, methods and relevant literature. A declaration covering doctoral status and the MSCA mobility rule. Certificate of language proficiency (see Hanken’s English language requirements at https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/language-requirement/english-language-requirements) Passport copy Academic text (at least 7000 words) Aptitude test or sufficient GPA (see requirements at: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/gpa-or-gmatgre ) Statement of Purpose written on Hankens template, see: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments), Please submit all application materials in English. Submit your application electronically via Hanken’s recruitment database Laura no later than by 11:59 p.m. on October 29th, 2026 (EET) . General instructions for applicants are provided here: https://www.hanken.fi/en/apply/application/phd-programme/attachments MSCA eligibility Applicants may be of any nationality. To be eligible for MSCA funding, the selected candidate must, on the first day of MSCA employment: (i) not hold a doctoral degree; candidates who have successfully defended a doctoral thesis but have not yet formally received the degree are not eligible; (ii) comply with the MSCA mobility rule, meaning they must not have resided or carried out their main activity (work, studies, etc.) in Finland for more than 12 months during the 36 months immediately preceding that date, excluding compulsory national service, short stays such as holidays, and time spent in a procedure for obtaining refugee status under the Geneva Convention; and (iii) be enrolled in, or meet the conditions required for timely enrolment in, the doctoral programme leading to the degree specified in this notice. The appointment is conditional on documentary verification of these conditions and fulfilment of the host institution's doctoral admission requirements. More information Questions about the project can be addressed to Mikko Vesa at mikko.vesa@hanken.fi . Questions about the application process can be sent to Hanken’s PhD Administration at admissions@hanken.fi . --- På svenska --- MSCA Doctoral Network EMANAIRE, DC 06: AI-samskapande, moral och det inre goda i de kreativa näringarna Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan, Institutionen för företagsledning och organisation, inbjuder ansökningar till detta fyraåriga doktorandstipendium inom projektet EMANAIRE. Doktorandprojektet har titeln ” AI-samskapande, moral och det inre goda i de kreativa näringarna ” . Om EMANAIRE EMANAIRE är ett Marie Skłodowska-Curie Doctoral Network som samlar 15 doktorander vid nio europeiska universitet för att studera hur AI förändrar arbetslivet. Projektet undersöker vad som händer när generativ och agentisk AI blir en del av ledarskap, dagliga arbetsflöden, teamkommunikation, professionellt lärande och karriärbeslut. Inom nätverket definieras mänsklig handlingsförmåga som den praktiska förmågan att förstå AI-stödda beslut, utöva omdöme, ifrågasätta resultat och påverka hur arbete organiseras. Varje doktorand blir en del av en internationell forskningsmiljö, får handledning över institutionsgränser och deltar i internatskolor, metodworkshoppar, månatliga forskningsseminarier och samarbete med organisationer utanför akademin. Varje projekt inkluderar dessutom aktivit engagemag med industripartner. Doktorandprojektet Vad händer med värdet och syftet med kreativt arbete när människor skapar tillsammans med AI? Projektet studerar hur AI-agenter, AI-medierade processer och plattformsalgoritmer omformar samskapande, moraliska frågor och affärsmodeller inom de kreativa näringarna. Projektet följer anställda, frilansare och kreativa studior när de hanterar förändringar i sitt arbete och sina affärsmodeller. Genom etnografiskt fältarbete kommer du att undersöka vad yrkesverksamma värdesätter i själva skapandeprocessen och hur detta förändras i mänskliga, hybrida och automatiserade arbetsformer. Projektet syftar till att utveckla en praktikbaserad förståelse av samskapande samt ge vägledning till organisationer och beslutsfattare som vill främja rättvist, ansvarsfullt och hållbart kreativt arbete Närmare information om arbetsuppgifter, handledning, utbildning och mobilitet samt vem vi söker och anställningsvillkor hittas i den engelska versionen av annonsen. Handledning och integrering vid Hanken Den utvalda kandidaten kommer att få nära handledning och kontinuerlig uppföljning av forskande fakultetsmedlemmar. Huvudhandledare är professor Mikko Vesa (Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan). Dessutom kommer den antagna doktoranden att tilldelas en till två bihandledare från EMANAIRE-nätverket . Doktoranden kommer att integreras i Institutionen för ledning och organisation samt i det bredare EMANAIRE-nätverket . Ytterligare information om doktorandprogrammet och antagningskraven finns via Hankens doktorandadministration: admissions@hanken.fi . Ansökan ska innehålla: Curriculum Vitae. Examensbevis och studieutdrag samt vid behov Diploma Supplement. Minst två akademiska eller professionella referenser. En forskningsplan på cirka 2 000 ord. Intyg om uppfyllande av MSCA:s mobilitetsregel. Intyg över engelska språkkunskaper. Kopia av pass. Akademisk text (minst 7 000 ord). Lämplighetstest eller tillräckligt GPA-värde. Statement of Purpose enligt Hankens mall. Samtliga ansökningshandlingar ska lämnas in på engelska. Skicka in din ansökan elektroniskt via Hankens rekryteringsdatabas Laura senast 29 oktober 2026 (EET) . MSCA-behörighet Sökande kan vara av vilken nationalitet som helst. För att vara berättigad till finansiering inom MSCA måste den utvalda kandidaten, på den första dagen av sin MSCA-anställning: Inte inneha en doktorsexamen. Kandidater som framgångsrikt har försvarat sin doktorsavhandling men ännu inte formellt tilldelats doktorsexamen är inte behöriga. Uppfylla MSCA:s mobilitetsregel, vilket innebär att kandidaten inte får ha varit bosatt eller bedrivit sin huvudsakliga verksamhet (arbete, studier etc.) i Finland under mer än 12 månader under de 36 månader som omedelbart föregår anställningens startdatum. Undantag gäller för obligatorisk nationell tjänstgöring, kortare vistelser såsom semester samt tid som tillbringats i en process för att erhålla flyktingstatus enligt Genèvekonventionen. Vara antagen till, eller uppfylla villkoren för att kunna antas inom utsatt tid till, det doktorandprogram som leder till den examen som anges i denna utlysning. Anställningen är villkorad av att dessa krav kan styrkas genom relevant dokumentation samt att värdinstitutionens krav för antagning till forskarutbildningen uppfylls. Kontakt Frågor om projektet: Mikko Vesa mikko.vesa@hanken.fi Frågor om ansökningsprocessen: admissions@hanken.fi Application period starts: 2026-09-16 13:00 Application period ends: 2026-10-29 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=401&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=406&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=lqs5z4g4q4gws80wg488swoswwcg0w4": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Sustainable and Resilient Freight Transport Systems",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher in Sustainable and Resilient Freight Transport Systems We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Postdoctoral Researcher in Sustainable and Resilient Freight Transport Systems [Se nedan för svenska] The Hanken School of Economics is looking for a postdoctoral researcher as a project researcher for 8 months to conduct research in the project S ociety Quest for a Resilient and Sustainable Nordic Freight Transport System Funded by the Peter Wallenberg Foundation, the project explores how to strengthen the resilience and environmental sustainability of Nordic freight transport and supply chains. Through parallel Society Quest processes in Finland and Sweden, researchers and societal stakeholders will jointly identify key challenges and develop priorities for future research, development, and Nordic collaboration. Society Quest is a structured co-creation method in which researchers, industry and public-sector actors move step by step from articulating a shared societal challenge to concrete directions for joint action. The position offers a unique opportunity to develop both your academic profile and your experience of working at the interface between research and practice. Postdoc responsibilities: Plan and carry out the Finnish Society Quest, in close collaboration with the Hanken and Linköping University research teams and supporting the Swedish implementation of the Society Quest. Map and engage relevant stakeholders across industry, public authorities, transport infrastructure actors, and the research community. Recruit Society Quest participants and coordinate stakeholder engagement Contribute to the design and facilitation of Society Quest co-creation workshops addressing resilient and environmentally sustainable freight transport. Systematically document and analyze findings in cooperation with the project researchers. Contribute to project dissemination. Preparation of journal manuscript(s) based on project results. The position includes some teaching responsibilities, up to 15 % of work time The successful candidate is expected to have: A doctoral degree in supply chain management, logistics, transportation, sustainability, or another relevant field. Knowledge of, or a strong research interest in, supply chain resilience, sustainable transport, freight transport, or closely related topics. Experience with qualitative and/or participatory research methods, for example, interviews, workshops, focus groups, co-creation, or stakeholder-engaged research. The ability to independently organize and carry out empirical research, including stakeholder identification, recruitment, data collection, documentation, and analysis. Strong stakeholder engagement and communication skills, with the ability to work with both academic and non-academic actors. Excellent written and oral English-language skills. Considered an advantage: Existing experience interacting with companies, public authorities, infrastructure actors, or other societal stakeholders. Experience with workshop facilitation or co-creation methodologies. Knowledge of resilience and sustainability research and their intersection. Finnish and/or Swedish language skills. Existing high-quality academic publications Teaching experience Industry experience Through the position, you will have the opportunity to: Contribute to a Nordic research project and shape its implementation. Develop expertise in resilient and sustainable freight transport. Build networks with academic, industry, and public-sector actors in Finland and Sweden. Gain experience in co-creation, stakeholder engagement, and cross-national research. Contribute to academic publications, societal impact, and the development of future research. Gain academic teaching experience. Eligibility criteria: Eligibility requirements: Applicants for this position are required to have (a) a PhD degree in a relevant subject and (b) a fluent command of English. Applicants close to their PhD defense can be considered if the defense date is decided. Possibility to start latest by February 2027. The position is for 8 months, depending on when you can start (earliest start: January 2027). By joining the Supply Chain Management & Social Responsibility subject at Hanken, you will benefit from and contribute to a thriving scientific environment at a triple crown-accredited university business school (AACSB, EQUIS, AMBA accreditations), becoming part of a group of highly active researchers with high productivity in publishing, numerous global projects, and a strong international profile. The annual working time in this position is 1612 hours. The location of the positions is in Helsinki ( https://www.hel.fi/en ), and we expect you to move to Finland. The salary for the project researcher is based on the university salary system in Finland (including employee healthcare as well as pension and holiday contributions); the exact salary level depends upon the recruited individual’s qualifications and performance. The entry-level salary is in the range of 46.800 - 52.500 euro/year. Benefits include occupational health care. The application should include the following attachments: Motivation letter stating how you’d contribute to the project CV incl. min. 2 references who can be contacted for recommendations PhD degree certificate Publication list incl. working doi links to selected, max 5 recent publications (or if links don’t work, separately submitted publications in pdf form) The application shall be submitted electronically to Hanken’s recruitment database Laura no later than November 16 th 2026 . In addition, other relevant documents (e.g. certificates, recommendations) may be submitted with the application. Please indicate when you would be able to start in the position if you should be selected. Enquiries may be directed to the project team: Associate Professor Anna Aminoff, anna.aminoff@hanken.fi Assistant Professor Helleke Heikkinen, helleke.heikkinen@hanken.fi The Hanken School of Economics reserves the right, for justified reasons, to leave the position open, to extend the application period, and to consider candidates who have not submitted applications during the application period. Hanken School of Economics reserves the right to close the application period early if a suitable candidate is identified and appointed. Further information: Project profiles under the ongoing projects of the HUMLOG Institute at http://www.hanken.fi/humloginstitute Hanken School of Economics: https://www.hanken.fi -- På svenska-- Postdoktoral forskare i hållbara och resilienta godstransportsystem Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan söker en postdoktoral forskare som projektforskare för 8 månader för att bedriva forskning inom projektet Samhällets strävan efter ett resilient och hållbart nordiskt godstransportsystem (Society Quest for a Resilient and Sustainable Nordic Freight Transport System). Projektet finansieras av Peter Wallenbergstiftelsen och undersöker hur resiliensen och den miljömässiga hållbarheten i nordiska godstransporter och försörjningskedjor kan stärkas. Genom parallella Society Quest-processer i Finland och Sverige kommer forskare och samhällsaktörer gemensamt att identifiera centrala utmaningar och utveckla prioriteringar för framtida forskning, utveckling och nordiskt samarbete. Society Quest är en strukturerad metod för samskapande där forskare, näringsliv och offentliga aktörer stegvis går från att formulera en gemensam samhällsutmaning till konkreta riktlinjer för gemensamma åtgärder. Tjänsten erbjuder en unik möjlighet att utveckla både din akademiska profil och din erfarenhet av att arbeta i gränslandet mellan forskning och praktik. Arbetsuppgifter Som postdoktor förväntas du: Planera och genomföra den finländska Society Quest-processen i nära samarbete med forskargrupperna vid Hanken och Linköpings universitet samt stödja genomförandet i Sverige. Kartlägga och engagera relevanta intressenter inom näringsliv, myndigheter, transportinfrastruktur och forskarsamhället. Rekrytera deltagare till Society Quest och koordinera intressenternas medverkan. Bidra till utformning och facilitering av samskapande workshoppar kring resilienta och miljömässigt hållbara godstransporter. Systematiskt dokumentera och analysera resultat tillsammans med projektets forskare. Bidra till projektets kommunikation och spridning av resultat. Förbereda vetenskapliga artiklar baserade på projektets resultat. Utföra undervisningsuppgifter motsvarande högst 15 % av arbetstiden. Kvalifikationer Den framgångsrika kandidaten förväntas ha: Doktorsexamen inom supply chain management, logistik, transporter, hållbarhet eller annat relevant område. Kunskap om, eller ett starkt forskningsintresse för, försörjningskedjors resiliens, hållbara transporter, godstransporter eller närliggande områden. Erfarenhet av kvalitativa och/eller deltagande forskningsmetoder, exempelvis intervjuer, workshoppar, fokusgrupper, samskapande processer eller intressentbaserad forskning. Förmåga att självständigt organisera och genomföra empirisk forskning, inklusive identifiering och rekrytering av intressenter, datainsamling, dokumentation och analys. God förmåga att samarbeta och kommunicera med såväl akademiska som icke-akademiska aktörer. Utmärkta kunskaper i engelska, både muntligt och skriftligt. Meriterande Erfarenhet av samarbete med företag, myndigheter, infrastrukturaktörer eller andra samhällsaktörer. Erfarenhet av att leda workshoppar eller arbeta med samskapandemetoder. Kunskap om forskning kring resiliens och hållbarhet samt samspelet mellan dessa områden. Kunskaper i finska och/eller svenska. Kvalificerade vetenskapliga publikationer. Undervisningserfarenhet. Erfarenhet från näringslivet. Du får möjlighet att Bidra till ett nordiskt forskningsprojekt och påverka dess genomförande. Utveckla expertis inom resilienta och hållbara godstransporter. Bygga nätverk med forskare, företag och offentliga aktörer i Finland och Sverige. Få erfarenhet av samskapande, intressentengagemang och gränsöverskridande forskning. Bidra till vetenskapliga publikationer, samhällsnytta och utveckling av framtida forskning. Skaffa akademisk undervisningserfarenhet. Behörighetskrav Sökande ska: Ha avlagt doktorsexamen inom ett relevant ämne. Behärska engelska flytande. Även sökande som ännu inte har disputerat kan beaktas om disputationsdatum redan har fastställts. Tillträde ska kunna ske senast i februari 2027. Om anställningen Tjänsten är tidsbegränsad till 8 månader , beroende på när du kan börja (tidigaste start januari 2027). Genom att ansluta dig till ämnesområdet Supply Chain Management & Social Responsibility vid Hanken blir du en del av en dynamisk vetenskaplig miljö vid en handelshögskola med så kallad Triple Crown -ackreditering (AACSB, EQUIS och AMBA). Du kommer att arbeta i en grupp av mycket aktiva forskare med hög publiceringstakt, omfattande internationella projekt och en stark internationell profil. Den årliga arbetstiden är 1 612 timmar . Arbetsorten är Helsingfors , och vi förutsätter att du flyttar till Finland. Lön och förmåner Lönen för projektforskaren följer det finländska universitetens lönesystem och omfattar företagshälsovård samt pensions- och semesterförmåner. Ingångslönen ligger inom intervallet 46 800–52 500 euro per år , beroende på den valda kandidatens kvalifikationer och prestationer. Ansökningshandlingar Ansökan ska innehålla: Motivationsbrev med beskrivning av hur du skulle bidra till projektet. CV inklusive minst två referenser som kan kontaktas. Examensbevis för doktorsexamen. Publikationsförteckning inklusive fungerande DOI-länkar till max fem utvalda, nyligen publicerade arbeten (alternativt publikationerna som separata PDF-filer om länkarna inte fungerar). Ytterligare relevanta dokument, såsom intyg och rekommendationer, kan bifogas. Ansökan Ansökan ska lämnas in elektroniskt via Hankens rekryteringssystem Laura senast 16 november 2026 . Ange även när du kan tillträda tjänsten om du blir vald. Kontaktpersoner Biträdande professor Anna Aminoff – anna.aminoff@hanken.fi Biträdande professor Helleke Heikkinen – helleke.heikkinen@hanken.fi Övrigt Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan förbehåller sig rätten att, av motiverade skäl, lämna tjänsten obesatt, förlänga ansökningstiden eller beakta kandidater som inte lämnat in ansökan under den ordinarie ansökningsperioden. Hanken förbehåller sig även rätten att avsluta rekryteringen tidigare om en lämplig kandidat identifieras och anställs. Mer information HUMLOG Institute: http://www.hanken.fi/humloginstitute Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan: https://www.hanken.fi/ Application period starts: 2026-10-22 15:00 Application period ends: 2026-11-16 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=406&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=407&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=lqs5z4g4q4gws80wg488swoswwcg0w4": {
      "title": "The position",
      "description": "Biträdande professor (nivå 1 eller 2, tenure track) i nationalekonomi / Assistant or Associate Professor (Tenure Track) in Economics We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Biträdande professor (nivå 1 eller 2, tenure track) i nationalekonomi / Assistant or Associate Professor (Tenure Track) in Economics (For English, see below) Svenska handelshögskolan (Hanken) ledigförklarar en befattning som biträdande professor (nivå 1 eller 2, tenure track) i nationalekonomi med tillträde senast i september 2027 eller enligt överenskommelse. Befattningen är placerad vid ämnet nationalekonomi i Helsingfors. Befattningen Sökande inom samtliga områden av nationalekonomi kommer att beaktas för anställningen som biträdande professor (nivå 1 eller 2). Viss preferens ges till sökande med inriktning på politisk ekonomi i bred bemärkelse. Undervisning på svenska förutsätts. Befattningen ingår i Hankens forskningsorienterade karriärstig (tenure track) och är öppen för personer med potential för en framstående vetenskaplig karriär. Den som anställs har möjlighet att avancera genom utvärdering av meriter inom alla relevanta områden i enlighet med Hankens tenure track riktlinjer . En anställning som biträdande professor (nivå 1) är tidsbunden för 5 år med möjlighet om att anhålla om en förlängning på 2 år. Befordran till biträdande professor (nivå 2) förutsätter en utvärdering i enlighet med Hankens tenure track riktlinjer. En anställning som biträdande professor (nivå 2) är tillsvidare. Nationalekonomi vid Hanken Hanken är en forskningsinriktad handelshögskola som erbjuder utbildning på svenska och engelska. Ämnet nationalekonomi bedriver högklassig undervisning och forskning, med särskilda styrkeområden inom industriell organisation, beteende- och experimentell ekonomi, arbetsmarknadsekonomi, samt empirisk och teoretisk mikroekonomi i bredare bemärkelse. Vi erbjuder heltäckande utbildning på kandidat-, magister- och doktorandnivå. Helsinki Graduate School of Economics Ämnet nationalekonomi vid Hanken är en aktiv partner i Helsinki Graduate School of Economics (Helsinki GSE). Helsinki GSE sammanför nationalekonomer från tre finländska universitet: Aalto-universitetet, Svenska handelshögskolan och Helsingfors universitet. Dess uppdrag är att bedriva framstående forskning med största möjliga akademiska och samhälleliga genomslag, utbilda nästa generation ekonomer på internationell toppnivå och erbjuda högklassig utbildning över ämnesgränserna. Helsinki GSE samarbetar nära med Statens ekonomiska forskningscentral VATT (https://www.vatt.fi/en/). Helsinki GSE erbjuder en mångsidig och aktiv forskningsmiljö med elva forskningsgrupper inom olika områden av nationalekonomi. Undervisningen inom Helsinki GSE samordnas mellan partneruniversiteten för att maximera genomslaget för studenterna och samhället. Hanken och Helsinki GSE är centralt belägna i Helsingfors. Här hittar du mera information om ämnet nationalekonomi och Helsinki GSE . Behörighetskrav Sökande bedöms utifrån forskning, undervisning, aktivitet inom den vetenskapliga gemenskapen och samhällelig påverkan. Den som söker anställning som biträdande professor (nivå 1) ska ha doktorsexamen i nationalekonomi eller ett närliggande område, eller vara nära att slutföra sin doktorsexamen. Särskild vikt läggs vid den sökandes potential att bedriva högklassig vetenskaplig forskning och ge högklassig undervisning i nationalekonomi. Utöver de krav som ställs på en biträdande professor (nivå 1), ska sökande till biträdande professor (nivå 2) ha uppnått och kunnat uppvisa internationellt hög nivå på sin forskning inom positionens vetenskapsområde, hög nivå i undervisningen och bidragit med att delta i gemensamma uppdrag vid universitet ( institutional service ) samt främjat samhällelig växelverkan. Som fristående handelshögskola med starka nordiska rötter erbjuder Hanken högklassiga examensprogram på svenska och engelska. Av sökande krävs flytande kunskaper i både engelska och svenska. Undervisning på svenska ingår i arbetsuppgifterna. Akademisk personal vid Hanken förväntas bedriva och handleda vetenskaplig forskning, ge högklassig akademisk undervisning, följa utvecklingen inom sitt område samt bidra till Hanken, den akademiska gemenskapen och samhället. Undervisningsuppgifterna fördelas utifrån ämnets behov i undervisningsplanen och den anställdas relevanta kompetens. Anställningen är på heltid och den årliga arbetstiden är 1612 timmar. Under läsåret förväntas den anställda vara anträffbar på institutionen i Helsingfors i genomsnitt minst tre dagar per vecka för att aktivt bidra till forsknings- och undervisningsmiljön. Hanken förutsätter att akademiska medarbetare bor och arbetar i Finland och erbjuder flyttstöd till personer som rekryteras från utlandet. Lön Lönen fastställs enligt lönesystemet för universiteten i Finland (företagshälsovård och pensions- och semesterpremier ingår i anställningen). Den exakta lönenivån beror på den anställdas kvalifikationer. Hanken stöder den valda kandidaten med en startbudget för forskning. Det är dessutom möjligt att ansöka om ytterligare anslag för forskning, resor och utveckling av undervisningen. Hanken belönar excellens inom både forskning och undervisning. Tilläggsinformation För ytterligare information, kontakta professor Topi Miettinen, topi.miettinen@hanken.fi . Allmänna anvisningar för sökande finns här . Mer information om Hanken som arbetsgivare finns här . Rekryteringsprocess och tidsplan Ansökningstiden går ut den 17 november 2026 . Intervjuer genomförs online efter ansökningstidens utgång inom ramen för European Job Market Online Interview Window den 14–17 december 2026. De kandidater som går vidare bjuds in till ett campusbesök som omfattar en intervju och en forskningspresentation. Hur ansöker man Ansökan ska riktas till rektor och innehålla följande handlingar: Ansökan där den sökande specificerar vilken position hen söker (biträdande professor, nivå 1 eller nivå 2) Meritförteckning (CV) inklusive publikationslista. Ett standardiserat Job Market-CV inom nationalekonomi är tillräckligt. En ofta använd CV-mall finns här . Ansökningsbrev som innehåller beskrivning av tidigare forskning, dess vetenskapliga kvalitet och akademiska påverkan, planer för framtida forskning och sökandes deltagande i gemensamma uppdrag (eng. institutional service ) vid den egna institutionen och universitetet samt kandidatens samhälleliga växelverkan. För sökande till biträdande professor (nivå 2) ska ansökningsbrevet även innehålla beskrivning av forskningssamarbete med andra forskare, kontribution till internationella vetenskapliga nätverk, engagemang i ansökningar om extern forskningsfinansiering och kontribution till den pedagogiska utvecklingen inom institutionen eller universitetet utöver den egna undervisningen. Ansökan ska vara skriven med den öppna positionen i åtanke. Kopior av fem forskningspublikationer som bäst demonstrerar forskning av hög vetenskaplig kvalitet. En undervisningsportfölj (för exempel på innehåll, se här ) Tre referensbrev från akademiska forskare. Breven lämnas in via EconJobMarket eller skickas direkt till Hanken på humanresources@hanken.fi . Samtliga ansökningshandlingar ska lämnas in på engelska via rekryteringsdatabasen LAURA. Ansökningstiden går ut den 17 november 2026. Om Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan, Hanken, placerar sig bland de ledande handelshögskolorna i Norden. Hanken finns i Finland med kampus i Helsingfors och Vasa. Hanken erbjuder program på kandidat-, magister- och doktorandnivå samt EMBA och Executive Development -program som går på svenska eller engelska.  Hanken har 2 725 kandidat- och magisterstuderande samt 118 doktorander. Universitetet har nära kontakt med näringslivet och ett aktivt alumnnätverk med över 13 800 alumner i mer än 70 länder. Hanken har de tre mest ansedda ackrediteringarna; AACSB, AMBA och EQUIS. Hanken finns rankad i Financial Times Masters in Management på plats 56 (2026). Hanken är även känt för sin högkvalitativa forskning, internationella inriktning och fokus på hållbarhet. ------------------------------- Hanken School of Economics invites applications for an Assistant or Associate Professor (tenure track) in Economics, with the appointment beginning no later than September 2027 (negotiable). The position is based in the Economics Unit in Helsinki. The position Candidates from all fields of economics will be considered for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor. Some preference will be given to candidates working in political economics, broadly defined. Teaching in Swedish is expected. The position is part of Hanken’s research-oriented tenure-track system and is open to individuals with the potential for an excellent scientific career. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to advance through evaluations that consider merits in all relevant areas in accordance with Hanken’s tenure track guidelines .  The Assistant Professor position is fixed-term for 5 years, with the possibility to apply for a 2-year extension. Promotion to Associate Professor is subject to a tenure evaluation in accordance with Hanken’s tenure track guidelines. The Associate Professor position is permanent. Economics at Hanken Hanken School of Economics is a research-oriented business school offering education in English and Swedish. Hanken’s Economics Unit is committed to high-quality teaching and research, with strengths in industrial organisation, behavioural and experimental economics, labour economics and empirical and theoretical microeconomics more broadly. We offer comprehensive undergraduate, master’s and doctoral programmes. Helsinki Graduate School of Economics Hanken’s Economics Unit is an active partner in the Helsinki Graduate School of Economics (Helsinki GSE). Helsinki GSE brings together economics faculty from three Finnish universities: Aalto University, Hanken School of Economics and the University of Helsinki. Its mission is to produce outstanding research with maximum academic and societal impact, educate the next generation of world-class economists, and offer excellent training across disciplinary boundaries. Helsinki GSE collaborates closely with the VATT Institute for Economic Research (https://www.vatt.fi/en/). Helsinki GSE offers a versatile and active research environment and hosts eleven research groups in various fields of economics. Teaching within Helsinki GSE is coordinated among its partner universities to maximise its impact on students and society. Hanken and Helsinki GSE are conveniently located in central Helsinki. For more information, please visit the Economics unit and Helsinki GSE . Requirements Applicants will be evaluated based on their research, teaching, institutional service and societal impact.  Applicants on the assistant professor level should hold a doctoral degree, or be close to completing one, in economics or a related field. Particular emphasis will be placed on applicants’ potential to conduct high-quality scientific research and provide high-quality teaching in economics. In addition to the requirements for an assistant professor, applicants for the associate professor level are expected to have demonstrated internationally high levels of research within the scientific field of the position, high levels in teaching and contributed through institutional service and societal impact. As an independent business school with strong Nordic roots, Hanken offers high-quality degree programmes in Swedish and English. Applicants for the current position are required to have a fluent command of both English and Swedish. Teaching in Swedish is expected as part of the position's responsibilities. Academic staff at Hanken are expected to conduct and supervise scientific research, provide high-quality academic teaching, remain abreast of developments in their field, and contribute to Hanken, the academic community and society. Teaching duties are allocated based on the curriculum needs of the subject and the appointee’s relevant expertise. The full-time position has an annual working time of 1,612 hours. During the academic year, the appointee is expected to work at the office in Helsinki for an average of at least three days per week to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment. Hanken requires academic employees to reside and work in Finland and provides relocation support for applicants moving to Finland from abroad. Salary The salary is determined in accordance with the salary system for Finnish universities and includes occupational health care as well as pension and holiday benefits. The exact salary level depends on the appointee’s qualifications. Hanken provides the selected candidate with a start-up research budget. Additional grants for research, travel and teaching development may also be applied for. Hanken rewards excellence in both research and teaching. Further information For further information, please contact Professor Topi Miettinen, topi.miettinen@hanken.fi . General instructions for applicants are available here . More information about Hanken as an employer is available here . Recruitment process and timeline The application deadline is 17 November 2026 . Candidates will be interviewed online after the application deadline in the European Job Market Online Interview Window, December 14-17, 2026. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to an on-campus visit that includes an interview and a research presentation. How to apply The application should be addressed to the Rector and must include: Cover letter in which the applicant specifies the position for which they are applying (associate professor or assistant professor) A curriculum vitae, including a list of publications. A standard economics Job Market CV is sufficient. One commonly used CV format is available at here . Personal statement describing the applicant’s previous research and its scientific quality and academic impact, plans for future research, service to the department and university, and societal impact. For candidates applying for the associate professor level, the personal statement should also include a description of research collaboration with other scholars, contributions to international scientific networks, involvement in applications for external research funding, and contributions to the pedagogical development in the department or university beyond own teaching. The personal statement needs to be written with the announced position in mind. Copies of five research publications that best demonstrate high scientific quality research A teaching portfolio (proposed content here ) Three letters of reference from academic researchers, submitted through EconJobMarket or sent directly to Hanken at humanresources@hanken.fi . If you apply for an associate professor position only, letters are not required but recommended. Please submit all application materials in English through Hanken’s recruitment database LAURA. The application deadline is 17 November 2026. About Hanken Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries. It is located in Finland, with campuses in Helsinki and Vaasa. Hanken offers a range of B.Sc., M.Sc., EMBA, PhD, and Executive Development programmes taught mainly in English and Swedish. Hanken has 2 725 Bachelor and Master’s students, and 118 Doctoral researchers. The School has close ties to the business community and an active alumni network with over 13 800 alumni working in more than 70 countries. The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. The Master’s programme was ranked 56 in the Masters in Management by Financial Times in 2026. Hanken is also recognized for its research quality, its international orientation, and its focus on sustainability. Application period starts: 2026-10-23 13:00 Application period ends: 2026-11-17 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=407&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=405&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=lqs5z4g4q4gws80wg488swoswwcg0w4": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (tenure-track) in Finance / Biträdande professor (nivå 1) i finansiell ekonomi (tenure track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (tenure-track) in Finance / Biträdande professor (nivå 1) i finansiell ekonomi (tenure track) We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Assistant Professor (tenure-track) in Finance / Biträdande professor (nivå 1) i finansiell ekonomi (tenure track) [Se nedan för svenska] Hanken School of Economics invites applications for an Assistant Professor (tenure-track) in Finance beginning no later than August 2027, or as otherwise agreed. The position is at the Finance Unit at the Department of Finance and Economics in Helsinki. For this position, we will consider candidates in all fields of Finance. The position is part of the Hanken tenure track system. It is open to talented individuals who have potential for an excellent scientific career. Individuals placed on the Hanken tenure track have the possibility to advance in their career through regular performance assessments, which consider their merits in all relevant qualification areas in accordance with Hanken’s tenure track guidelines . Hanken School of Economics is a research-oriented business school offering education in English and Swedish. Hanken’s Finance unit is committed to high-quality teaching and research. We offer full scale graduate and undergraduate programs. We have a strong research climate, reflected in a growing volume and range of research activities. We value high-quality, practice-oriented research, as evidenced by our publications in top-ranked journals. In addition, Hanken's Finance unit is an active partner in the Graduate School of Finance (GSF), which offers the national doctoral program in finance. GSF also organizes seminars and workshops for faculty members and doctoral students. Requirements The applicants will be reviewed based on their research, teaching, institutional service, and societal impact. Applicants should hold a doctoral degree (or be near completion of the doctorate) in Finance (or a related field). When evaluating the applicants’ qualifications, the main focus will be on the potential to conduct high-quality scientific research and the potential to provide high-quality teaching. A focus on asset pricing is considered a strong merit. Being a stand-alone business school with strong Nordic roots, Hanken offers degree programmes in Swedish and English. For this position, applicants are required to have fluent command of English, knowledge of Swedish is considered a merit. Hanken supports its faculty in learning the Swedish language, which serves as the administrative language of the business school. Academic staff at Hanken are expected to carry out and supervise scientific research, provide academic teaching, closely follow the advances of their field, and contribute service to Hanken, the academic community, and society.  Teaching tasks are allocated based on the curriculum needs of the subject and by considering relevant expertise. The full-time position has an annual working time of 1612 hours. During the academic year, it is expected that a minimum average of three days per week is spent at the office in Helsinki to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment. Hanken requires academic employees to reside and work in Finland, and it offers relocation support for applicants coming from outside Finland. Salary The salary is based on the university salary system in Finland (includes employee healthcare as well as pension and holiday contributions). The exact salary level depends on the recruited individual’s qualifications. Hanken will support the selected employee with a start-up research budget, and additional research, travel and teaching development grants can also be applied for. Hanken rewards excellence in both research and teaching. For more Information For additional information, please contact Head of Department Jesper Haga ( jesper.haga@hanken.fi) or Head of Subject Karl Felixson ( karl.felixson@hanken.fi) . General instructions for applicants are provided here . Also, read more about Hanken as an employer here . Recruitment process and timeline The application deadline is 22 November 2026 . Selected candidates will be interviewed online shortly after the application deadline. Short-listed candidates will be invited to on-site campus visits including an interview and research presentation. How to apply The application is to be addressed to the Rector and application materials should include: CV (proposed content here ), including list of publications. Personal statement, which includes a description of past research and its scientific quality, academic impact, plans for future research and a description of the candidate’s service to the department and university and a description of the candidate’s societal impact. Teaching portfolio (proposed content here ). Copies of no more than five research publications, including a ‘job market’ paper Three letters of reference from academic researchers, to be submitted via Econjobmarket or directly to Hanken via humanresources@hanken.fi . Please submit all application materials in English in Hanken’s recruitment database LAURA. The application deadline is 22 November 2026 . Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries. It is located in Finland, with campuses in Helsinki and Vaasa. Hanken offers a range of B.Sc., M.Sc., EMBA, PhD, and Executive Development programmes taught mainly in English and Swedish. Hanken has 2 725 Bachelor and Master’s students, and 118 Doctoral students. The School has close ties to the business community and an active alumni network with over 13 800 alumni working in more than 70 countries. The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. The Master’s programme was ranked 56 in the Masters in Management by Financial Times in 2026. Hanken is also recognized for its research quality, its international orientation, and its focus on sustainability. ---------------- Svenska handelshögskolan (Hanken) söker en biträdande professor (nivå 1) i finansiell ekonomi (tenure track) med start senast i augusti 2027 eller enligt överenskommelse. Befattningen är placerad vid ämnet finansiell ekonomi inom Institutionen för finansiell ekonomi och nationalekonomi i Helsingfors. För denna befattning beaktar vi kandidater inom alla områden av finansiell ekonomi. Befattningen ingår i Hankens forskningsorienterade karriärstig (tenure track). Den är öppen för kvalificerade kandidater med potential för en framstående vetenskaplig karriär. Kandidater som anställs inom Hankens tenure track-system har möjlighet till avancemang inom systemet genom utvärdering av meriter och prestationer inom alla relevanta områden i enlighet med Hankens riktlinjer . Svenska handelshögskolan är en forskningsinriktad handelshögskola som erbjuder utbildning på engelska och svenska.  Ämnet finansiell ekonomi vid Hanken är engagerat i högkvalitativ undervisning och forskning. Vi erbjuder program på både kandidat- och magisternivå. Vi har en stark forskningsmiljö, vilket återspeglas i en växande omfattning och bredd av forskningsverksamheten. Vi värdesätter högkvalitativ, praktiskt orienterad forskning, vilket framgår av våra publikationer i ledande vetenskapliga tidskrifter. Dessutom är ämnet finansiell ekonomi vid Hanken en aktiv partner i Graduate School of Finance (GSF), som erbjuder det nationella doktorandprogrammet i finansiell ekonomi. GSF arrangerar även seminarier och workshops för undervisande och forskande personal samt doktorander. Behörighetskrav Sökande bedöms utifrån forskning, undervisning, aktivitet inom den vetenskapliga gemenskapen och samhällelig påverkan. Sökande ska ha doktorsexamen i finansiell ekonomi (eller närliggande område) eller vara i slutskedet av sina doktorandstudier. Vid bedömningen ligger huvudfokus på potentialen att bedriva vetenskaplig forskning av hög kvalitet samt att ge undervisning av hög kvalitet. Specialisering inom tillgångsprissättning (asset pricing) betraktas som en stark merit. Som en fristående handelshögskola med stark nordisk förankring erbjuder Hanken utbildningsprogram på svenska och engelska. För befattningen krävs flytande kunskaper i engelska. Kunskaper i svenska betraktas som en merit. Hanken stöder sin personal i att lära sig svenska, som är handelshögskolans administrativa språk. Den akademiska personalen vid Hanken förväntas bedriva och handleda vetenskaplig forskning, ge akademisk undervisning, följa utvecklingen inom sitt ämnesområde samt delta i gemensamma uppdrag vid Hanken, den akademiska gemenskapen och samhället. Undervisningsuppgifter fördelas enligt undervisningsbehovet i ämnet samt den undervisande personalens expertis. Anställningen är på heltid och den årliga arbetstiden är 1612 timmar.  Under läsåret förväntar vi oss att du är anträffbar på institutionen i Helsingfors i genomsnitt minst tre arbetsdagar i veckan för att aktivt bidra till forsknings- och undervisningsmiljön. Hanken förutsätter att akademisk personal är bosatt och arbetar i Finland och erbjuder flyttstöd till personer som rekryteras från utlandet. Lön Lönen baserar sig på lönesystemet för universiteten i Finland (företagshälsovård och pensions- och semesterpremier ingår i anställningen). Den exakta lönenivån beror på den anställdas kvalifikationer. Hanken stöder nyanställd akademisk personal med en individuell startbudget för forskningen. Det finns möjlighet att ansöka om ytterligare forsknings-, rese- och undervisningsutvecklingsanslag. Hanken belönar excellens inom både forskning och undervisning. Tilläggsinformation För ytterligare information, vänligen kontakta prefekt Jesper Haga ( jesper.haga@hanken.fi ) eller ämnesansvarig Karl Felixson ( karl.felixson@hanken.fi ). Allmänna anvisningar till sökande hittar du här . Du kan också läsa mer om Hanken som arbetsgivare här . Rekryteringsprocess och tidtabell Sista ansökningsdag är den 22 november 2026. Utvalda kandidater intervjuas online kort efter ansökningstidens utgång. Kortlistade kandidater bjuds in till ett campusbesök som inkluderar en intervju samt en forskningspresentation. Ansökan Ansökan ska riktas till rektor och innehålla: CV (för exempel på innehåll, se här ), inklusive en publikationslista. Ansökningsbrev som inkluderar en beskrivning av tidigare forskning och dess vetenskapliga kvalitet, akademisk påverkan, planer för framtida forskning, en beskrivning av den sökandes deltagande i gemensamma uppdrag vid den egna institutionen och universitetet samt en beskrivning av kandidatens samhälleliga växelverkan. En undervisningsportfölj (för exempel på innehåll, se här ). Kopior av högst fem forskningspublikationer inklusive ett ”arbetsmarknadspapper” (eng. job market paper) Tre referensbrev från akademiska forskare som skickas via Econjobmarket eller direkt till Hanken via humanresources@hanken.fi . Samtliga ansökningshandlingar ska lämnas in på engelska via Hankens rekryteringssystem LAURA. Sista ansökningsdag är den 22 november 2026. Svenska handelshögskolan, Hanken, placerar sig bland de ledande handelshögskolorna i Norden. Hanken finns i Finland med kampus i Helsingfors och Vasa. Hanken erbjuder program på kandidat-, magister- och doktorandnivå samt EMBA och Executive Development -program som går på svenska eller engelska.  Hanken har 2 725 kandidat- och magisterstuderande samt 118 doktorander. Universitetet har nära kontakt med näringslivet och ett aktivt alumnnätverk med över 13 800 alumner i mer än 70 länder. Hanken har de tre mest ansedda ackrediteringarna; AACSB, AMBA och EQUIS. Hanken finns rankad i Financial Times Masters in Management på plats 56 (2026). Hanken är även känt för sin högkvalitativa forskning, internationella inriktning och fokus på hållbarhet. Application period starts: 2026-10-19 08:00 Application period ends: 2026-11-22 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=405&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    },
    "https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=397&key=&o=A_RJ&rspvt=lqs5z4g4q4gws80wg488swoswwcg0w4": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Management & Organisation / Biträdande professor (tenure track, nivå 1) i företagsledning och organisation",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Management & Organisation / Biträdande professor (tenure track, nivå 1) i företagsledning och organisation We use cookies to improve the user experience of the service and for statistics. By selecting \"Accept all\" you give your consent to the use of cookies. Modify settings Necessary (required cookies for the service to work) Statistics (cookies that measure the use of the service) på svenska Back to the job list Want to update your application? Log in. Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Management & Organisation / Biträdande professor (tenure track, nivå 1) i företagsledning och organisation The Department of Management and Organization at Hanken School of Economics invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor (tenure track) in Management & Organization The position is in Helsinki, starting August 1, 2027, or as agreed. Hanken School of Economics is one of the leading business schools in the Nordic countries, and recognized for its international orientation and outstanding research quality The School is accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS. We have close ties to the business community and an active alumni network. Our master's programme is ranked 56 in the Masters in Management 2026 by Financial Times. We are located in Helsinki and Vaasa. Finland is ranked as one of the best-governed countries in the world (Legatum prosperity index, 2023), as well as the happiest country in the world (World Happiness Report 2026). The city of Helsinki ranks as one of the most liveable cities in the world (The Economist 2024). These are thanks to, among others, the high level of equality and safety; free, high-quality education at both primary, secondary, and university levels; affordable healthcare and childcare; and competitiveness and innovativeness of the business sector. The Department of Management & Organization nurtures a strong community of researchers and teachers. We have a strong research climate, reflected in the volume and diversity of research activities, including externally funded projects, publications in highly ranked academic journals, an active community of PhD researchers, and a wide range of societal impact activities. Our goal is to conduct high-quality academic research with corporate and societal relevance. The focus of our research is broad and includes areas such as organizational behaviour, people management/HRM, strategy and strategic management, AI and technology, responsibility and sustainability, and more. Our scholars engage in active collaboration with other universities and business schools around the world. Scholars associated with the subject regularly publish articles in leading international academic journals such as the Journal of Management, Organization Studies, Academy of Management Review, Strategic Management Journal, Journal of International Business Studies, Journal of Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, Human Relations and Journal of Business Ethics . Our diversity is also reflected in our courses and programme at Bachelor, Master and PhD level. The teaching covers issues within organizational behavior, HRM, strategic management, international business, social responsibility and sustainability, and business ethics. At Hanken, our goal is to educate responsible professionals for the global economy and changing society. We embrace Hanken values in teaching and learning, such as openness, equality, and integrity, and promote an innovative learning community that answers to the challenges of the global world, and that efficiently integrates students, faculty, staff, the corporate world, as well as partner organizations and universities. More information about our teaching and research can be found here: https://www.hanken.fi/en/departments-centres/department-management-and-organisation Requirements Applicants must have a doctoral degree (or be very near completion of the doctorate). The degree can be from any relevant discipline provided that the candidate’s research focus is related to the area of management and organization. A focus on organizational behavior or HRM is considered a merit. Candidates will be reviewed based on their research, teaching, institutional service, and societal impact. The main focus will be on the potential to conduct high-quality scientific research, , and the potential to provide high-quality teaching. Research is the most important of the qualification areas followed by teaching, and then, service and societal impact. Applicants for the current position are required to have a fluent command of both English and Swedish. Teaching in Swedish is expected as part of the position's responsibilities. Academic staff at Hanken are expected to carry out and supervise scientific research projects, obtain external funding, provide high-quality academic teaching, closely follow the advances of their field, and participate in service to Hanken, the larger academic community, and society. The full-time position has an annual working time of 1612 hours. During the academic year, it is expected that a minimum average of three days per week is spent at the office in Helsinki to actively contribute to the research and teaching environment, as well as to the collegial community. Hanken offers relocation support for tenure track professors coming outside Finland and expects full-time academic employees to reside and work in Finland. Teaching tasks are allocated based on the curriculum needs of the subject and by considering relevant expertise. Hanken offers multiple pedagogical training opportunities as well as Swedish language training. Salary and other benefits The salary is based on the university salary system in Finland. The exact salary level depends on qualifications and performance. At the assistant professor level, the annual salary range starts from around 60.000 euros (including a holiday bonus). In addition, the employment includes occupational healthcare as well as pension contributions. Hanken will support the appointed person with a research budget and additional rewards for excellence in research and teaching. Research, travel, and teaching development grants can also be applied for. Individuals placed on the Hanken tenure track have the possibility to advance in their career through regular performance assessments, which take into account their merits in all relevant qualification areas of the tenure track system. Interviews Short-listed candidates will be invited to on-site campus visits including an interview and research presentation. Other arrangements are possible for short-listed candidates not based in Europe. For more information For additional information, please contact Professor Mats Ehrnrooth, Head of Department, mats.ehrnrooth@hanken.fi How to apply The application is to be addressed to the Rector and application materials should include: Cover letter CV, including a list of publications (proposed content here ) Personal statement, which includes a description of past research and its scientific quality, academic impact, plans for future research, a description of the candidate’s service to the department and university, and a description of the candidate’s societal impact Copies of no more than five research publications, including a ‘job market’ paper which is an original piece of research by the candidate that constitutes their best research to date Portfolio (e.g., Teaching portfolio template ) Three letters of reference from academic researchers to be submitted directly to Hanken via humanresources@hanken.fi Relevant certificates (degree certificates, language certificates) Please submit all application materials in English. Please note that only applications submitted through the database will be considered. Full applications should be submitted through the link below no later than November 30, 2026 . General instructions for applicants are provided here . Also, read more about Hanken as an employer here . ******** Institutionen för företagsledning och organisation söker en Biträdande professor (tenure track, nivå 1) i företagsledning och organisation Befattningen är placerad i Helsingfors och anställningen börjar 1.8.2027 eller enligt överenskommelse. Hanken Svenska handelshögskolan är en av de ledande handelshögskolorna i Norden, och är erkänd för sin internationella orientering och framstående forskningskvalitet i förhållande till sin storlek. Högskolan är ackrediterad av AACSB, AMBA och EQUIS. Vi har nära band till näringslivet och ett aktivt alumninätverk. Vårt magisterprogram rankas på plats 56 i Financial Times ranking Masters in Management 2026. Vi finns i Helsingfors och Vasa. Finland rankas som ett av de bäst styrda länderna i världen (Legatum Prosperity Index, 2023), samt som världens lyckligaste land (World Happiness Report 2026). Helsingfors rankas som en av världens mest levnadsvänliga städer (The Economist 2024). Detta tack vare bland annat den höga nivån av jämställdhet och trygghet; gratis utbildning av hög kvalitet på både grundskole-, gymnasie- och universitetsnivå; prisvärd hälso- och sjukvård samt barnomsorg; samt näringslivets konkurrenskraft och innovationsförmåga. Institutionen för företagsledning och organisation har en stark gemenskap av forskare och lärare vars forskningsaktiviteter har ett brett fokus som omfattar områden som organisationsbeteende, personalledning/HRM, strategi och strategisk ledning, AI och teknologi, företagsansvar och hållbarhet, med mera. Vi har ett starkt forskningsfokus som återspeglas i en ökande volym och mångfald av forskningsaktiviteter, inklusive externt finansierade projekt, publikationer i högt rankade akademiska tidskrifter, en aktiv gemenskap av doktorander, och olika aktiviteter med social och samhällelig relevans. Våra forskare publicerar regelbundet sin forskning i ledande internationella akademiska tidskrifter som Journal of Management, Organization Studies, Strategic Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Journal of International Business Studies, Journal of Organizational Behavior, Human Resource Management, Human Relations och Journal of Business Ethics . Vår mångfald återspeglas också i våra kurser och program på kandidat-, magister-, och doktorandnivå. Vår undervisning präglas av variation och täcker frågor inom personaladministration och HRM samt strategi och strategisk ledning, internationellt företagande, ansvar, hållbarhet och företagsetik. Vid Hanken är vårt mål att utbilda ansvarsfulla yrkesutövare för den globala ekonomin och det föränderliga samhället. Vi omfamnar Hanken värderingar i undervisning och lärande, såsom öppenhet, jämlikhet och integritet, och främjar en mångsidig och innovativ lärandegemenskap som svarar på globala utmaningar och som effektivt integrerar studenter, fakultet, personal, näringslivet samt samarbetsorganisationer och universitet. Mer information om forskningen och undervisningen inom ämnet företagsledning finns på: https://www.hanken.fi/sv/institutioner-center/institutionen-foretagsledning-och-organisation Krav Sökande måste ha en doktorsexamen (eller bevisligen vara i slutskedet av sina doktorandstudier). Doktorsexamen kan vara från olika akademiska discipliner förutsatt att kandidatens forskningsfokus är relaterat till området företagsledning och organisation. Ett fokus på organisationsbeteende eller HRM är meriterande. Sökande kommer att granskas baserat på deras forskning, undervisning, institutionstjänstgöring och samhällspåverkan. Huvudfokus ligger på potentialen att bedriva högkvalitativ vetenskaplig forskning och på potentialen att tillhandahålla högkvalitativ undervisning. Forskning är det viktigaste av behörighetsområdena följt av undervisning och sedan gemensamma uppdrag vid universitetet samt samhällelig växelverkan. Sökande förväntas ha flytande kunskaper i både engelska och svenska. Undervisning på svenska förväntas inom ramen för tjänsten. Akademisk personal vid Hanken förväntas bedriva och handleda vetenskaplig forskning, erhålla extern finansiering, tillhandahålla högkvalitativ akademisk undervisning, noggrant följa utvecklingen inom sitt område och bidra till Hanken, den akademiska gemenskapen och samhället. Heltidsbefattningen har en årlig arbetstid på 1612 timmar. Under läsåret förväntar vi oss att du är anträffbar på institutionen i Helsingfors minst tre arbetsdagar i veckan för att aktivt bidra till forsknings- och undervisningsmiljön, samt till arbetsgemenskapen på institutionen. Hanken erbjuder flyttstöd åt forskardoktorer (tenure track) som kommer från länder utanför Finland och förväntar sig att heltidsanställd akademisk personal bor och arbetar i Finland. Undervisningsuppgifter tilldelas utgående från ämnets behov och lärarens expertis. Hanken erbjuder flera pedagogiska utbildningsmöjligheter samt utbildning i svenska språket. Lön och förmåner Lönen baserar sig på lönesystemet för universiteten i Finland. Den exakta lönenivån beror på kvalifikationer och prestationsnivå. På forskardoktornivå är årslönens utgångsnivå cirka 60 000 euro (inklusive semesterpremie). Hanken stöder forskardoktorn med en budget för forskningen. Man kan ansöka om ytterligare forsknings-, rese- och undervisningsutvecklingsanslag. Dessutom ingår företagshälsovård och pensionspremier i anställningen. Hanken belönar excellens inom forskning och undervisning. Personer som anställs på Hankens tenure track har möjlighet att främja sin karriär genom regelbundna prestationsbedömningar som beaktar deras meriter inom alla relevanta kvalifikationsområden i tenure track-systemet Intervjuer Utvalda kandidater kommer att bjudas in till besök på campus som innefattar en intervju och en forskningspresentation. Andra arrangemang kan ordnas för valda kandidater som inte är bosatta i Europa. Tilläggsinformation För ytterligare information, vänligen kontakta professor Mats Ehrnrooth, Prefekt , mats.ehrnrooth@hanken.fi . Hur ansöka Ansökningar riktas till Hankens rektor och ansökningshandlingar ska inkludera följande dokument: Ansökningsbrev CV inklusive en publikationslista (förslag till uppställning här ) Personlig redogörelse som beskriver tidigare forskning och dess vetenskapliga kvalitet, akademiskt inflytande, planer för kommande forskning, en redogörelse över den sökandes aktivitet inom institutionen och den vetenskapliga gemenskapen samt en redogörelse för den sökandes samhälleliga påverkan Max 5 forskningspublikationer, inklusive ett s.k. ’job market paper’ som utgörs av kandidatens mest framstående originalforskning/primärforskning hittills Undervisningsportfölj (t.ex. Teaching portfolio -model ) Tre rekommendationsbrev av akademiska forskare skall skickas in direkt till Hanken via humanresources@hanken.fi Relevanta diplom och intyg (examensintyg, språkintyg) Vänligen lämna in ansökningshandlingarna på engelska. Observera att endast ansökningar inlämnade via rekryteringsdatabasen beaktas. Sista ansökningsdagen är den 30 november 2026. Allmänna instruktioner för sökande finns här . Läs också mer om Hanken som arbetsgivare här . Application period starts: 2026-09-15 16:30 Application period ends: 2026-11-30 23:59 Submit an application Share Direct link to the job: https://hanken.rekrytointi.com/paikat/index.php?jid=397&o=A_RJ Privacy policy Accessibility Cookies"
    }
